    "title": "Witcher 3 Remastered: Reviews, Switch 2, Steam Deck",
    "headline": "Witcher 3 Grades In:\nSwitch 2 Wins, Deck Wobbles",
    "subhead": "The reviews are glowing and the Switch 2 port is being called a standout. The Steam Deck numbers say CD Projekt's 'runs just fine' line needs an asterisk.",
    "description": "Witcher 3 Remastered reviews are in: 9/10s, a standout Switch 2 port, and Steam Deck tests showing a 5-10 fps drop against the original. Here's the report card.",
    "keywords": [
      "Witcher 3 Remastered",
      "Witcher 3 Remastered review",
      "Witcher 3 Steam Deck",
      "Witcher 3 Switch 2",
      "CD Projekt Red",
      "Witcher 3 free upgrade",
      "single-player RPG",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "WITCHER 3 GRADES IN:\nSWITCH 2 WINS, DECK WOBBLES",
    "ogAccent": "3A7D44",
    "trendScore": 80,
    "heroCredit": "RPG Site",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.rpgsite.net/feature/21472-the-witcher-3-remastered-switch-2-review-vs-original-graphics-comparison-features-upgrade",
    "body": "The upgrade went live Tuesday, and the argument that ran all last week about how it looks has a new question attached to it: how does it run? Reviews say great. Handheld testing says it depends on the handheld.\n\n## The critics\n[Pure Xbox's roundup](https://www.purexbox.com/news/2026/09/roundup-the-first-reviews-are-in-for-the-witcher-3-remastered) put the early scores side by side: Metro gave it 4.5 out of 5, and Noisy Pixel, GamingBolt and GameTyrant each landed on 9 out of 10. Polygon and Sportskeeda came in positive, PCGamesN mostly positive. The main knock, from Noisy Pixel: facial animations and some interactions look older next to the upgraded environments. Metro's read was that the remaster keeps the skeleton of the original intact instead of rebuilding it.\n\n## Switch 2 is the surprise\n[RPG Site's Switch 2 analysis](https://www.rpgsite.net/feature/21472-the-witcher-3-remastered-switch-2-review-vs-original-graphics-comparison-features-upgrade) called it the biggest upgrade the reviewer has seen for a Switch 2 version of a Switch 1 game, and the best Switch 2 port of 2026. The load-time gap is real: fast travel took about 42 to 43 seconds against 110 on the original Switch, and loading a save took 27 to 29 seconds against 51. The complaint is handheld image quality. It targets 40fps but looks notably softer than expected, and the reviewer is hoping for a 30fps quality mode in a patch.\n\n## The Steam Deck part\n[RPG Site's Steam Deck testing](https://www.rpgsite.net/feature/21474-the-witcher-3-remastered-steam-deck-performance-recommended-settings-vs-original-oled) went the other way. On the same preset, the remaster ran roughly 5 to 10 fps lower than the original, which held 40-plus. In a demanding area like Novigrad it dipped to around 30. The reviewer also says motion blur is too strong by default and should be turned off. Two fair caveats: that testing was done before launch on Proton Experimental, and final AMD drivers weren't available yet, so numbers could improve. CD Projekt's own line was that the game runs [just fine on Steam Deck and Switch 2](https://gamingbolt.com/the-witcher-3-wild-hunt-remastered-runs-just-fine-on-steam-deck-and-switch-2-per-cdpr). Playable and identical aren't the same word.\n\n## What it means for the lane\nSingle-player RPG people play on handhelds. A free upgrade that costs you frames on the Deck and wins big on Switch 2 is a real decision, not a footnote. Check the settings before you blame the game.\n\n## The cultural read\nEleven years after launch, people are still tuning frame rates for The Witcher 3. That's what a benchmark looks like. Every big-world RPG that's shipped since has been measured against it, and this week the measuring tape came out again.\n\n## Sources\n- [Pure Xbox review roundup, Sept. 28, 2026](https://www.purexbox.com/news/2026/09/roundup-the-first-reviews-are-in-for-the-witcher-3-remastered)\n- [RPG Site: Switch 2 version](https://www.rpgsite.net/feature/21472-the-witcher-3-remastered-switch-2-review-vs-original-graphics-comparison-features-upgrade)\n- [RPG Site: Steam Deck performance, Sept. 28, 2026](https://www.rpgsite.net/feature/21474-the-witcher-3-remastered-steam-deck-performance-recommended-settings-vs-original-oled)\n- [GamingBolt on CD Projekt's statement](https://gamingbolt.com/the-witcher-3-wild-hunt-remastered-runs-just-fine-on-steam-deck-and-switch-2-per-cdpr)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
