    "body": "Six words, early Sunday morning, and a lot of people did math. Rod Wave and NBA YoungBoy on the same stadium stage is the kind of idea fans have been floating for a while. This time, one of the two said something.\n\n## What was actually said\nDJ Akademiks posted publicly calling for a joint tour and collaboration between the two. Rod Wave replied on X in the early hours of Sunday, Sept. 27: \"I told yb we going stadium.\" That's from [Rolling Out's write-up](https://rollingout.com/2026/09/28/rod-wave-stadium-tour-with-nba-youngboy/), which is clear that nothing else came with it. [HOT 97](https://www.hot97.com/news/rod-wave-told-nba-youngboy-their-doing-a-stadium-tour/) ran the same headline framing. [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/articles/news) listed it Sept. 27 as a stadium tour tease.\n\n## What isn't there\nNo dates. No venues. No promoter, no announcement from YoungBoy's side. It's a tease, and it should be read as one. Rolling Out also points to the logistics: YoungBoy is currently living outside the United States, which would be the first thing any U.S. stadium plan has to solve.\n\n## Why people care anyway\nThese are two of the most loyal fanbases in melodic and Southern rap. When artists with that kind of streaming pull talk about stadiums, it moves the conversation about who can actually fill one without a pop crossover. Fans don't need a press release to start buying flights in their heads.\n\n## The cultural read\nHip-hop's biggest touring stories used to come from the radio. Now they come from a reply under somebody else's post. Watch for a real announcement. Until then, it's six words and a lot of hope.\n\n## Sources\n- [Rolling Out, Sept. 28, 2026](https://rollingout.com/2026/09/28/rod-wave-stadium-tour-with-nba-youngboy/)\n- [HOT 97](https://www.hot97.com/news/rod-wave-told-nba-youngboy-their-doing-a-stadium-tour/)\n- [HotNewHipHop news feed, Sept. 27, 2026](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/articles/news)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
