    "ogHeadline": "WITCHER 3 BREAKS ITS\nOWN STEAM RECORD",
    "ogAccent": "3A7D44",
    "trendScore": 84,
    "heroCredit": "Kotaku",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://kotaku.com/the-witcher-3-remastered-just-broke-a-steam-record-as-people-rush-back-to-play-a-new-and-improved-version-of-one-of-the-best-rpgs-ever-2000738418",
    "body": "Eleven years after it shipped, the oldest big-world RPG in the room just had its biggest night. Not a sale night. A players-online night.\n\n## The number\n[TweakTown](https://www.tweaktown.com/news/113814/the-witcher-3-wild-hunt-remastered-breaks-the-games-all-time-steam-player-record/index.html), citing SteamDB, has The Witcher 3 peaking at 120,975 concurrent players on Sept. 29, the day the Remastered upgrade went live. The old record was 103,329, set in January 2020. [Kotaku](https://kotaku.com/the-witcher-3-remastered-just-broke-a-steam-record-as-people-rush-back-to-play-a-new-and-improved-version-of-one-of-the-best-rpgs-ever-2000738418) had it past 120,000 and still climbing when it filed, so the final peak could sit a little higher than the figure above.\n\n## Why this launch pulled harder\nTwo things stacked. The Remastered upgrade is free for people who already own the game, so the whole back catalog of owners had a reason to reinstall. And per Kotaku, the base game was half off at launch, which gave everyone who never bought it a reason to start. Kotaku also points out that Steam was a smaller store in 2020, especially in markets like China, and that the 2023 next-gen console update never came near these numbers.\n\n## What the number can't tell you\nConcurrent players is a snapshot of who's online at the same minute. It's Steam only. It doesn't count console players on PS5, Xbox or Switch 2, and it isn't a sales figure. A free upgrade brings back people who already paid CD Projekt years ago. It's a loyalty number as much as a growth number. Both are good news. They're just different news.\n\n## Where it sits with the reviews\nWe covered the report card already: [the reviews were strong and the handheld numbers came with asterisks](/the-lane/witcher-3-remastered-reviews-steam-deck-novigrad-30fps-switch-2-best-port-2026). The record is the other half of that story. Critics grade it. The player count votes on it.\n\n## The cultural read\nSingle-player RPG fans get told all the time that the genre is niche. A game from 2015 just outdrew every day it's ever had on the biggest PC storefront. That's not niche. That's a standard people keep measuring new games against, and this week the standard set its own bar again.\n\n## Sources\n- [TweakTown: Witcher 3 Remastered breaks the game's all-time Steam player record](https://www.tweaktown.com/news/113814/the-witcher-3-wild-hunt-remastered-breaks-the-games-all-time-steam-player-record/index.html)\n- [Kotaku: The Witcher 3 Remastered just broke a Steam record](https://kotaku.com/the-witcher-3-remastered-just-broke-a-steam-record-as-people-rush-back-to-play-a-new-and-improved-version-of-one-of-the-best-rpgs-ever-2000738418)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
