    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamingbolt.com/gta-6-team-admits-pressure-is-huge-but-wouldnt-compromise-at-all-everything-is-dialed-up",
    "body": "Every GTA 6 headline this week has been a feature list. This one's a mindset, and it comes from the person who'd know.\n\n## What Garbut said\nAaron Garbut, co-studio head at Rockstar North, talked about the pressure on the project in Game Informer's cover story, as [GamingBolt reported Sept. 30](https://www.gamingbolt.com/gta-6-team-admits-pressure-is-huge-but-wouldnt-compromise-at-all-everything-is-dialed-up). His words: the pressure for the team is huge. The answer, he says, was to over-deliver. Instead of trading one thing for another, the studio pushed detail, scope, breadth, scale, interaction and density all at once. He also says he doesn't think Rockstar has made anything close to this before.\n\n## What \"dialed up\" looks like on paper\nThe same cover story has already produced a run of specifics. GamingBolt's coverage this week lists six regions with Vice City rebuilt and expanded, more than 170 animal species, and a weather system with moving storms and hurricanes. Read next to Garbut's quote, the list makes sense. Nobody trims a project when the plan is to answer pressure with more.\n\n## The clock\nGrand Theft Auto VI launches Nov. 19 on PS5 and Xbox Series X|S. From Oct. 1 that's 49 days. The last stretch before a launch this size is usually quiet on the studio side and loud on everyone else's.\n\n## What it doesn't say\nGarbut doesn't promise anything specific, and neither does this article. \"Over-deliver\" describes the goal, not the result. We'll know which one it is in seven weeks.\n\n## The cultural read\nMost studios talk about pressure like it's a weather report. Rockstar's saying it plainly, and saying it out loud is a small flex: we know what this is, we know what it has to be, and we didn't cut a corner to make the date. Whether that lands is a November question. The confidence is a September fact.\n\n## Sources\n- [GamingBolt: GTA 6 team admits pressure is huge](https://www.gamingbolt.com/gta-6-team-admits-pressure-is-huge-but-wouldnt-compromise-at-all-everything-is-dialed-up)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
