    "heroCreditUrl": "https://x.com/urltv/status/2105103652054618557",
    "body": "Tay Roc fought in Atlanta on Sept. 27. Four weeks later he's booked for London. URL doesn't let the room cool off.\n\n## The announcement\n[Ultimate Rap League's post on X](https://x.com/urltv/status/2105103652054618557) is short: Tay Roc vs Illmac, London, England, October 25th, \"Night of Main Events.\" That's the whole announcement. The post doesn't list the rest of the card, ticket details or how the show will be streamed, so none of that is confirmed.\n\n## The tape is out\nSummer Madness XVI is [out now on the URLTV app](https://x.com/urltv/status/2105018588415316348), and URL is asking fans to name their favorite battle in the comments. URL billed the event as sold out and called the Tay Roc and Rum Nitty rematch the most anticipated in battle rap history. We're not calling a winner here. Watch the tape and decide for yourself.\n\n## Why the turnaround matters\nTwenty-eight days between Atlanta and London is quick for a headliner at this level. It says URL sees Roc as the name that sells a Night of Main Events, and it keeps him in the conversation while Summer Madness XVI is still being argued about online. In a culture that runs on debate, staying booked is staying relevant.\n\n## What's still open\nThe opponent's side of the story, the rest of the London card, and the format. Illmac's name on the poster is the only confirmed detail besides the date and city. Watch @urltv for the follow-up.\n\n## The cultural read\nBattle rap is a Black-built art form that's been running its own economy for years: its own league, its own app, its own calendar. URL taking a main event overseas is a reminder of how far that model travels without a mainstream label pushing it. The room in London gets the same thing Atlanta got. Bars, no filter, no delay.\n\n## Sources\n- [Ultimate Rap League on X: Tay Roc vs Illmac, London, Oct. 25](https://x.com/urltv/status/2105103652054618557)\n- [Ultimate Rap League on X: Summer Madness XVI out now on the URLTV app](https://x.com/urltv/status/2105018588415316348)\n- [Ultimate Rap League on X: Summer Madness XVI sold out](https://x.com/urltv/status/2103500291567980791)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
