      "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.sneakerfiles.com/air-jordan-14-forest-green/",
      "heroFocus": "center",
      "body": "The Air Jordan 14 Forest Green releases October 31, 2026, at $215 under style code 487471-300. Per SneakerFiles, it's the first time the original colorway has been retroed.\n\nWhite leather upper, perforations, rib stitching across the panels. Green hits the midsole, the Ferrari-inspired emblem, and the branding. Black accents, a carbon-fiber shank plate, mostly white rubber underneath. SneakerFiles also notes the 2026 pair runs on an updated shape that sits closer to the OG than past 14 retros. Hedge that until in-hand photos land, because \"closer to OG\" is Jordan Brand's promise and the toe box will tell the truth.\n\n## Why the 14 keeps getting a second look\n\nThe 14 is the shoe Michael Jordan wore for the 1998 Finals, and it's still the one with the clearest design story: Tinker Hatfield pulled from Jordan's Ferrari. Go back to our [Last Shot history](/the-lane/air-jordan-14-last-shot-june-14-1998-retro-cycle-history) for the full run. Forest Green is the quiet cousin of that moment. No title-winning shot attached, just a clean white-and-green pair that people remember from the early-2000s rotation.\n\n## Where it drops\n\nSneakerFiles lists Nike, Finish Line, Foot Locker, Champs, DSG, Shiekh, Shoe Palace, and JD Sports. That's a wide general release, which tells you where this one sits. Not a scarcity play. A wear-it pair on a holiday weekend.\n\nIf you've been watching the 14 lately, the Mowalola collab [went wide in September](/the-lane/mowalola-air-jordan-14-wide-release-september-26-snkrs-second-chance-2026). Forest Green is the opposite energy: no designer, no story to sell, just the shoe.\n\n## The read\n\nPrice is the only real friction. $215 for a 14 is where the line has settled. If the shape lands, it's fair. If it doesn't, the resale market will say so within a week. Buy it to wear it.\n\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated from San Diego. Run by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.\n\n## Sources\n- [SneakerFiles, Air Jordan 14 Forest Green, Aug. 23, 2026](https://www.sneakerfiles.com/air-jordan-14-forest-green/)\n- [SneakerFiles, Air Jordan release dates, accessed Oct. 3, 2026](https://www.sneakerfiles.com/air-jordan-release-dates/)\n",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-03",
      "goLiveAt": "2026-10-03"
