    "title": "Rick Ross Arrested in Miami Beach on Felony Battery Charge",
    "headline": "Rick Ross Arrested\nin Miami Beach",
    "subhead": "Ross surrendered Thursday on a felony battery-by-strangulation charge tied to an Aug. 28 incident at his Star Island home. He says the allegations are fabricated. A judge set bond at $5,000 and told his lawyer she had no idea who he was.",
    "description": "Rick Ross turned himself in Oct. 1 on felony battery by strangulation and misdemeanor battery. What the affidavit says, what Ross says, and what's next on Oct. 22.",
    "keywords": [
      "Rick Ross",
      "Rick Ross arrested",
      "Miami Beach police",
      "battery by strangulation",
      "Judge Mindy Glazer",
      "Star Island",
      "Jazzma Kendrick",
      "50 Cent",
      "hip-hop news",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "RICK ROSS ARRESTED\nIN MIAMI BEACH",
    "ogAccent": "B3001B",
    "trendScore": 97,
    "heroCredit": "CBS News Miami",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.cbsnews.com/miami/news/rick-ross-arrested-miami-beach-battery-strangulation/",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "heroImage": "https://assets2.cbsnewsstatic.com/hub/i/r/2026/10/01/a50cea9d-d492-4938-a4be-b3832427c98d/thumbnail/1200x630/54cef233ea57d862eb190389b03c0f90/cbsmiami-rick-ross-arrest-miami-beach-1.jpg",
    "body": "The biggest hip-hop story of the week is a police report. Rick Ross, 50, walked into Miami Beach Police headquarters on Thursday, Oct. 1, and left in custody.\n\n## What he's charged with\nPer [CBS News Miami](https://www.cbsnews.com/miami/news/rick-ross-arrested-miami-beach-battery-strangulation/), William Leonard Roberts II surrendered to detectives Thursday morning and was booked into Turner Guilford Knight Correctional Center at 6:10 a.m. The charges: one felony count of battery by strangulation and one misdemeanor count of battery, both filed as domestic violence. The alleged incident happened Aug. 28 at his Star Island home. The woman reported it to police on Sept. 29.\n\n## What the affidavit says\nThe arrest affidavit, as reported by CBS Miami and [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011669-rick-ross-domestic-police-report-details), says the woman had been in a relationship with Ross for about a year and was living with him. She told police he woke her around 7:44 a.m. angry that she'd been tagged in an Instagram photo, slapped her, and later struck her in the chest, twisted the collar of her hoodie to restrict her breathing, pulled her by the ponytail into a wall and hit her in the face, splitting her lip. Police say she gave a sworn statement and timestamped photos of her injuries, and that home surveillance showed a friend arriving to pick her up and being turned away. These are allegations. Ross has pleaded not guilty.\n\n![Rick Ross booking photo via XXL](https://townsquare.media/site/812/files/2026/10/attachment-rick-ross-mugshot-header.jpg?w=1200&format=natural \"XXL|https://www.xxlmag.com/rick-ross-arrested-for-allegedly-choking-slapping-ex-girlfriend/\")\n\n## \"I have no idea who you are\"\nRoss appeared in Miami-Dade bond court by Zoom. His attorney, Bradley Horenstein, noted that his client is a celebrity and asked for an expedited release. Circuit Judge Mindy Glazer, per [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011577-rick-ross-lawyers-statement), answered: \"I have no idea who you are.\" Bond was set at $4,000 on the felony and $1,000 on the misdemeanor. She also issued a stay-away order covering the alleged victim's home, work and social media, and ordered Ross to surrender his firearms. He bonded out before noon and said he was flying to Dubai and Paris for weekend shows. Arraignment is Oct. 22.\n\n## What Ross says\nOn Instagram Stories around noon: \"I'm totally innocent of the fabricated allegations made against myself.\" Attorneys Steve Sadow and Horenstein said in a statement that Ross \"is being wrongfully accused by an ex-girlfriend whose true motivations are unclear,\" and pointed out the report was filed a month after the alleged incident. [XXL](https://www.xxlmag.com/rick-ross-arrested-for-allegedly-choking-slapping-ex-girlfriend/) names the accuser as Jazzma Kendrick, who [posted injury photos and accused Ross days earlier](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/jazzma-kendrick-accuses-rick-ross-assault-instagram-story-50-cent-reacts-no-response-september-27-2026). Police have not publicly confirmed the woman's identity.\n\n![Rick Ross's lawyers respond via HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/imgprst/2292x1200-fit-81-auto/2026/10/rick-ross-lawyers-respond-scaled.jpg \"HotNewHipHop|https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011577-rick-ross-lawyers-statement\")\n\n## The noise around it\n50 Cent posted \"LOL ARRESTED,\" because of course he did. [CNN](https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/01/entertainment/rapper-rick-ross-arrested) carried it nationally. For a man whose entire brand is the Boss who never loses, the image of him on a Zoom bond call being told he's nobody special is the part the culture will remember, whatever the courts decide.\n\n## The read\nA felony charge is not a conviction, and Ross will get his day in court. What's already true is that the case now has a docket number, a stay-away order and an Oct. 22 date. For the women in his orbit, and for the artists who've watched Boosie, Durk and Thug learn the hard way that a filing follows you, the lesson doesn't need a verdict.\n\n## Sources\n- [CBS News Miami, Oct. 1, 2026: Rick Ross arrested after woman accuses rapper of strangling, hitting her at Miami Beach home](https://www.cbsnews.com/miami/news/rick-ross-arrested-miami-beach-battery-strangulation/)\n- [XXL, Oct. 1, 2026: Rick Ross arrested for allegedly choking and slapping ex-girlfriend](https://www.xxlmag.com/rick-ross-arrested-for-allegedly-choking-slapping-ex-girlfriend/)\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 1, 2026: Judge denies Rick Ross special treatment; lawyers' statement](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011577-rick-ross-lawyers-statement)\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 1, 2026: Police report details](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011669-rick-ross-domestic-police-report-details)\n- [CNN, Oct. 1, 2026: Rapper Rick Ross arrested on domestic violence charges](https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/01/entertainment/rapper-rick-ross-arrested)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
