    "slug": "eminem-kid-rock-7-sins-confirmed-complex-halfway-2-jesus-foreword-nerds-nycc-marshalls-massacre-october-2-2026",
    "pillar": "hiphop",
    "title": "Eminem's Kid Rock Feature Is Real, and Kid Rock Explains It",
    "headline": "Eminem's Kid Rock\nFeature Is Confirmed",
    "subhead": "Complex confirmed through Eminem's camp that '7 Sins' is an official track on Kid Rock's Christian rock album. The foreword frames it as two Detroit friends who disagree politically. Fans are split. Separately, Eminem has an NYCC capsule coming and an arcade game that's already playable.",
    "description": "Eminem's '7 Sins' feature on Kid Rock's Halfway 2 Jesus is confirmed by his camp, per Complex. Kid Rock's foreword, the backlash, the date dispute, and Em's NYCC drop with NERDS.",
    "keywords": [
      "Eminem",
      "Kid Rock",
      "7 Sins",
      "Halfway 2 Jesus",
      "Eminem Kid Rock feature",
      "NERDS Clothing",
      "Marshall's Massacre",
      "New York Comic Con",
      "Detroit",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "EMINEM'S KID ROCK\nFEATURE IS CONFIRMED",
    "ogAccent": "1F3A5F",
    "trendScore": 84,
    "heroCredit": "Complex (Kevin Sabitus/Getty; Gary Miller/Getty)",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.complex.com/music/a/will-lavin/eminem-kid-rock-friendship-politics-7-sins-new-track",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "heroImage": "https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/c_crop,h_977,w_1735,x_0,y_0/g_auto:aoi_344_96_347_195,ar_1.91,c_fill,q_auto,w_1200/sanity-new/geaopsp4lmkvrqrcjmlr",
    "body": "When Kid Rock posted a tracklist Thursday with Eminem on a song called \"7 Sins,\" the first reaction from Em's base was that it had to be fake. It isn't.\n\n## The confirmation\n[Complex](https://www.complex.com/music/a/will-lavin/eminem-kid-rock-friendship-politics-7-sins-new-track) confirmed through a representative from Eminem's camp that \"7 Sins\" is an official track on Kid Rock's 13th album, the Christian rock record he's calling Halfway 2 Jesus. Complex also obtained a piece of the album's foreword. Kid Rock: \"I'm proud of the guests who joined me, especially my old friend Eminem. His verse speaks to something we've talked about and that really needs to be heard: we differ politically and on other things, but we've stayed friends through it all.\" He adds that they \"hope that sets an example for people who've lost friends or stopped talking to family because they think differently.\"\n\n## Why people doubted it\nEminem spent the back half of the last decade on the other side of the aisle from Kid Rock, including the 2017 BET cypher ultimatum to his own fans, per [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011657-eminem-kid-rock-7-sins-feature-backlash), and a 2024 appearance at a Kamala Harris rally in Detroit. So when the Shadyverse fan page shared the tracklist, the replies were \"No f*ing way,\" \"FAKE,\" and a theory that Kid Rock had dug up an old verse, per [Complex's first report](https://www.complex.com/music/a/will-lavin/eminem-kid-rock-fans-question-new-music-halfway-2-jesus-7-sins). Other fans pointed at the obvious: both from Detroit, and they've done this before. \"Fuck Off\" was on Kid Rock's Devil Without a Cause in 1998, and Rock cameoed in the \"Berzerk\" video in 2013.\n\n!youtube(https://youtu.be/ab9176Srb5Y)\n\n## The date dispute\n[HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011739-kid-rock-eminem-controversial-feature-album) lists the album for Oct. 17. Complex says no release date has been announced. Treat the 17th as unconfirmed until Kid Rock's camp says it. The lead single, \"James 1:17 (Jesus Is King),\" has a video out as of Thursday night. The album also lists Rascal Flatts' Gary LeVox and Jimmie Allen among the 17 tracks.\n\n![Eminem via HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/imgprst/2292x1200-fit-81-auto/2026/10/eminem-e1790898814763.jpg \"HotNewHipHop|https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011657-eminem-kid-rock-7-sins-feature-backlash\")\n\n## Meanwhile, at Comic Con\nSeparate Eminem news, same day. [Complex Style](https://www.complex.com/style/a/treyalston/eminem-nerds-clothing-marshalls-massacre-new-york-comic-con) reports a NERDS Clothing capsule sold only at the brand's booth, No. 3253, during New York Comic Con, Oct. 8 to 11: a skate deck, a long-sleeve tee, a lightweight bomber, hand-embellished arcade pieces by NYC artist Danny Cortes, and an original game called Marshall's Massacre, developed by Fan Arcade and already live. NERDS has done Astro Boy, Street Fighter and Sonic before. Eminem joins that list.\n\n![Eminem x NERDS Clothing via Complex](https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/c_crop,h_1081,w_1919,x_0,y_0/g_auto:aoi_838_127_384_216,ar_1.91,c_fill,q_auto,w_1200/sanity-new/vdrfjcbviqloscxuemns \"Complex|https://www.complex.com/style/a/treyalston/eminem-nerds-clothing-marshalls-massacre-new-york-comic-con\")\n\n## The read\nNobody has heard the verse. A feature credit tells you who's in the room, not what was said in it. The argument that matters starts when the song does. Until then, the only confirmed fact is the one Complex nailed down: Em chose to be on it.\n\n## Sources\n- [Complex, Oct. 2, 2026: Eminem and Kid Rock prioritize friendship over politics on new track](https://www.complex.com/music/a/will-lavin/eminem-kid-rock-friendship-politics-7-sins-new-track)\n- [Complex, Oct. 1, 2026: Eminem fans think Kid Rock feature announcement is fake](https://www.complex.com/music/a/will-lavin/eminem-kid-rock-fans-question-new-music-halfway-2-jesus-7-sins)\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 2, 2026: Kid Rock speaks on Eminem](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011739-kid-rock-eminem-controversial-feature-album)\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 1, 2026: Eminem gets pushback over upcoming Kid Rock feature](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011657-eminem-kid-rock-7-sins-feature-backlash)\n- [Complex, Oct. 2, 2026: Eminem teams with NERDS Clothing for NYCC merch and video game collab](https://www.complex.com/style/a/treyalston/eminem-nerds-clothing-marshalls-massacre-new-york-comic-con)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
