    "slug": "air-jordan-3-middle-east-ix6986-047-official-images-arabic-23-mosaic-print-holiday-2026-regional-exclusive",
    "pillar": "sneakers",
    "title": "First Look: Air Jordan 3 'Middle East' Swaps Elephant Print for Mosaic",
    "headline": "Air Jordan 3 'Middle East'\nOfficial Images",
    "subhead": "IX6986-047 lands Holiday 2026, reportedly only in Middle Eastern markets: Soft Pearl leather, Pomegranate trim, '23' embroidered in Arabic on the tongue, embossed mosaic geometry where the elephant print goes, and a burgundy box.",
    "description": "Official images of the Air Jordan 3 'Middle East' (IX6986-047): Arabic '23' on the tongue, mosaic embossing instead of elephant print, Holiday 2026, reportedly region-exclusive.",
    "keywords": [
      "Air Jordan 3 Middle East",
      "IX6986-047",
      "Air Jordan 3",
      "Jordan Brand regional exclusive",
      "Air Jordan 3 2026",
      "zSneakerHeadz",
      "Holiday 2026",
      "Air Jordan 3 Katrina",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "AIR JORDAN 3 'MIDDLE EAST'\nOFFICIAL IMAGES",
    "ogAccent": "6B1E2A",
    "trendScore": 80,
    "heroCredit": "Sneaker News / Nike",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/02/air-jordan-3-middle-east-ix6986-047/",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "heroImage": "https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/air-jordan-3-middle-east-IX6986-047-1.jpg",
    "body": "A day after Nike told Wall Street it wants the Jumpman [scarce again](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/nike-ceo-elliott-hill-jordan-retro-releases-cut-2027-back-to-scarcity-model-q1-fy27-earnings-call-october-1-2026), the first shoe that fits the new script surfaced: an Air Jordan 3 you can't buy here.\n\n## The shoe\nAir Jordan 3 \"Middle East,\" style IX6986-047, in Soft Pearl/Mink Brown/Light Orewood Brown/Pomegranate, per [JustFreshKicks](https://justfreshkicks.com/air-jordan-3-middle-east-ix6986-047/). Official images came through [@zSneakerHeadz on Instagram](https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/air-jordan-3-middle-east-release-date-ix6986-047), with @SneakerMarketRO reporting a Holiday 2026 launch through select retailers. [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/02/air-jordan-3-middle-east-ix6986-047/) calls it \"the region's first true exclusive\" and expects it to stay in Middle Eastern markets. Price is unconfirmed; Sole Retriever and Sneaker Bar Detroit list $215 and December, JustFreshKicks files both as unconfirmed by Jordan Brand.\n\n## The details\nThe elephant print is gone. In its place: embossed mosaic geometry on the toe and heel, which Complex reads as Islamic-art patterning. The tongue carries \"ithnaan\" and \"thalatha,\" Arabic for two and three, so the 23 is there if you can read it, and it's debossed again at the forefoot. Nike Air on the heel, a notched Jumpman under the laces, an extra set of burgundy laces, a leather Jumpman hangtag, and a burgundy \"23\" box with the Jumpman on the lid. Sneaker News sees the \"Katrina\" blocking in the base and a possible A Ma Maniére \"Burgundy Crush\" echo in the trim.\n\n![Air Jordan 3 \"Middle East\" lateral via JustFreshKicks](https://justfreshkicks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/air-jordan-3-middle-east-ix6986-047-lateral.jpg \"JustFreshKicks / Nike|https://justfreshkicks.com/air-jordan-3-middle-east-ix6986-047/\")\n\n## The pattern\nSneaker News ties it to the earnings call: executives talked about streamlining regions and chasing local demand, and the Air Jordan 11 \"City Pack\" and Air Jordan 4 \"London\" were the first signs. Men's sizing only in the images; no GS or kids' pairs listed. JustFreshKicks notes some European retailers have run raffles for past regional pairs, so expect that path rather than SNKRS US.\n\n![Air Jordan 3 \"Middle East\" via House of Heat](https://cdn.sanity.io/images/pu5wtzfc/production/920871ad8f1d1464751c590745cabd67568ef84c-2000x1250.png?rect=0,100,2000,1050&w=1200&h=630 \"House of Heat|https://houseofheat.co/jordan/air-jordan-3-middle-east-ix6986-047\")\n\n## The read\nTinker's elephant print is the most protected texture in the line, and Jordan Brand just replaced it with a regional pattern for a region that buys Jordans at full price and rarely gets a story of its own. That's the scarcity model in practice: a real shoe, a real market, and a U.S. buyer paying a resale premium to get in. Katrina colors, Gulf audience, Beaverton margins.\n\n## Sources\n- [Sneaker News, Oct. 2, 2026: First look at the Air Jordan 3 \"Middle East\"](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/02/air-jordan-3-middle-east-ix6986-047/)\n- [Complex, Oct. 2, 2026: This Air Jordan 3 pays homage to the Middle East](https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/air-jordan-3-middle-east-release-date-ix6986-047)\n- [JustFreshKicks, Oct. 2, 2026: Air Jordan 3 \"Middle East\" surfaces in official images](https://justfreshkicks.com/air-jordan-3-middle-east-ix6986-047/)\n- [House of Heat, Oct. 2, 2026: Air Jordan 3 \"Middle East\" IX6986-047](https://houseofheat.co/jordan/air-jordan-3-middle-east-ix6986-047)\n- [Sneaker Bar Detroit, Oct. 2, 2026: Air Jordan 3 \"Middle East\" official photos](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/air-jordan-3-middle-east/)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-10-02",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-10-02"
