    "ogHeadline": "DRUSKI GETS THE TIME\nCOVER. YE SALUTES.",
    "ogAccent": "C8102E",
    "trendScore": 76,
    "heroCredit": "TIME / Stefano Giuliano",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://time.com/collection/time100-next/2026/druski/",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "heroImage": "https://static.time.com/v3/assets/bltea6093859af6183b/blt1fe3fd89ca5749dc/6ab55c32a2444173098225df/t100next_i_druski_web_003.jpg?branch=production&width=1601&quality=75&auto=webp&crop=16:9%2Coffset-x100.00%2Coffset-y39.89",
    "body": "Druski has played a record executive, a megachurch pastor and a NASCAR patriot. This week he played himself on the cover of TIME.\n\n## The cover\nDruski fronts the 2026 TIME100 Next list, revealed Sept. 30. [TIME's tribute](https://time.com/collection/time100-next/2026/druski/) is written by Mark Wahlberg, who says the two are \"in serious talks about making a comedy together\" and predicts Druski \"will probably be one of the most powerful guys in the industry\" in ten years. Art direction by Jana Frost, photography by Stefano Giuliano; the separate cover interview is by Lucy Feldman, per [Complex](https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/tracewilliamcowen/druski-kanye-west-time-magazine-congratulations). In that interview he says he's \"no politician... just a funny guy,\" which is what you say when your characters keep getting read as commentary.\n\n## The Ye exchange\nYe shared the cover to his Instagram Stories with one word: \"Congratulations.\" Druski replied \"Thank you Kanye\" with a salute, then posted a clip from the 2007 HBO pilot Ye made with Larry Charles, the Curb-style show that never aired. In the clip Ye argues with a woman who doesn't believe he's associated with TIME: \"I've actually never been on the cover of VIBE. I was on TIME... You never heard of it? TIME?\" Twenty years later, the joke pays off on someone else's cover.\n\n!youtube(https://youtu.be/LroAUA7bqxg)\n\n## The movie\nLivestream From Hell, the horror-comedy with Kai Cenat and Kevin Hart, with Sexyy Red as herself, is out now on Prime Video, per Complex. Kai's week went [a different direction](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/kai-cenat-says-hes-suing-reggie-rakai-denies-allegations-clover-boys-ray-leaves-september-30-2026), but the film is live.\n\n![Druski and Ye via Complex](https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/c_crop,h_1081,w_1920,x_0,y_0/g_auto:aoi_768_433_384_216,ar_1.91,c_fill,q_auto,w_1200/sanity-new/wbfc2njxbq3lemygqy9s \"Complex / Getty|https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/tracewilliamcowen/druski-kanye-west-time-magazine-congratulations\")\n\n## The read\nDruski built an audience on Instagram sketches that the industry he parodies now hires him to make. A TIME cover is the mainstream catching up to a thing Black Twitter settled years ago. The Wahlberg co-sign and the Prime Video release are the part that pays. The Ye clip is the part that's funny.\n\n## Sources\n- [TIME, Sept. 30, 2026: Druski, TIME100 Next 2026](https://time.com/collection/time100-next/2026/druski/)\n- [Complex, Oct. 1, 2026: Druski shares clip of Ye's unreleased HBO pilot after congratulations over TIME cover](https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/tracewilliamcowen/druski-kanye-west-time-magazine-congratulations)\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 1, 2026: Druski and Ye's TIME exchange](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011640-druski-kanye-time-congratulations-throwback)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
