    "heroCredit": "uDiscover Music / Universal Music",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.udiscovermusic.com/news/quavo-qromelife/",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "heroImage": "https://www.udiscovermusic.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/quavo-qromelife.jpg",
    "body": "[HotNewHipHop's Friday list](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011571-hip-hop-albums-songs-october-2-2026) calls it a light one, and it is. Fourth quarter is when labels close the checkbook and save the budget for next year. Here's what actually came out.\n\n## The headliner\nQuavo, QRÖMELIFE. Fourteen tracks, all Pharrell, with Offset, Future, Lil Baby, Tyler, Rocky, T.I., Yung Miami and Justin Timberlake. We covered [what Quavo said about 2027](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/quavo-complex-interview-three-migos-takeoff-projects-2027-tyler-top-25-verse-qromelife-reviews-october-2-2026) and the first reviews. Start with \"Baby Breath\" and \"Away.\"\n\n!youtube(https://youtu.be/9fEoyWlR83s)\n\n## The anniversary\nMac Miller, The Divine Feminine (10-Year Deluxe). The 2016 album with Anderson .Paak, Kendrick, Ariana Grande and CeeLo gets bonus tracks for its tenth birthday. [Ratings Game Music](https://ratingsgamemusic.com/2026/10/02/mac-miller-the-divine-feminine-10th-anniversary-album-review/) reviewed it day-one. The estate has been careful with Mac's catalog since Balloonerism; this is the romantic record, not the heavy one.\n\n## The R&B lane\nVictoria Monét, Frequency of Love: 22 tracks, SZA among the guests, and the follow-up to Jaguar II after a Grammy run. Ari Lennox, Vacancy: Late Checkout, extends the Vacancy project. Zacari, Let It Ride. Lalah Hathaway, Made in Chicago.\n\n## The rap lane\nNoCap, Heaven On Mars. Russ, Come Back To Me. Armani Caesar, The Liz Symphony, the Griselda first lady's new one. OMB Peezy, What She Wants. Joey Trap, TRAPHOUSE BENTLEY. BLP Kosher, Grip Thumb 2 Paper Cuts. Quadeca, Life 1, which was already out before Friday.\n\n## The producer record\nWondaGurl, NORTH OF EVERYTHING. The Toronto producer behind Travis, Rihanna and Jay-Z records drops her own project. Producer albums rarely get the push; this one deserves the listen.\n\n## The singles\nLil Nas X, \"World's Greatest!,\" [his first since his mother's death](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/lil-nas-x-worlds-greatest-video-late-mother-tamikia-hill-phillip-youmans-atlanta-october-1-2026). Yung Miami, \"2008\" and \"F U,\" ahead of [Watch Dis on Oct. 23](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/yung-miami-watch-dis-debut-solo-album-october-23-2008-f-u-singles-quavo-g-herbo-lil-baby-kodak-vybz-kartel-2026). Skip Waiters with SWAVAY, \"MR. PIKS.\"\n\n![Lil Nas X \"World's Greatest!\" via XXL](https://townsquare.media/site/812/files/2026/10/attachment-lil-nas-x-worlds-greatest.jpg?w=1200&format=natural \"XXL / Lil Nas X on YouTube|https://www.xxlmag.com/lil-nas-x-worlds-greatest-video/\")\n\n## The read\nOne major-label rap album, one estate reissue, one R&B contender and a lot of independents. That's October now. The money shows back up on the 23rd. Until then the independents own the Friday, which is the only time of year they get it.\n\n## Sources\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 1, 2026: Hip-hop albums and songs dropping Oct. 2, 2026](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011571-hip-hop-albums-songs-october-2-2026)\n- [uDiscover Music, Oct. 2, 2026: Quavo releases QRÖMELIFE](https://www.udiscovermusic.com/news/quavo-qromelife/)\n- [Ratings Game Music, Oct. 2, 2026: Mac Miller, The Divine Feminine (10th Anniversary) review](https://ratingsgamemusic.com/2026/10/02/mac-miller-the-divine-feminine-10th-anniversary-album-review/)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
