    "ogHeadline": "CHAINSAW MAN CROCS\nDROP FIRST AT NYCC",
    "ogAccent": "E63946",
    "trendScore": 74,
    "heroCredit": "Sneaker News / Crocs",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/29/chainsaw-man-crocs-classic-clog/",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "heroImage": "https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/chainsaw-man-crocs-classic-clog.jpg",
    "body": "Crocs has figured out that anime fans will wear the joke. Chainsaw Man is the most literal version yet.\n\n## The collection\nFour Classic Clogs, per [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/29/chainsaw-man-crocs-classic-clog/). The Chainsaw Man pair is red and black with a chainsaw-shaped attachment running across the upper, jagged teeth and all, mimicking Denji's transformed head. Pochita's is yellow with a smaller chainsaw off the toe. Power's is blue, red and white with her horns extending from the heel strap and a red necklace-style accessory draped over the top. The fourth is a black clog loaded with Jibbitz referencing the series. [CBR](https://www.cbr.com/chainsaw-man-crocs-collection-foot-locker-nycc-release/) has the pricing from Foot Locker's release: $69.99 for the Chainsaw Man, Power and Characters clogs, $79.99 for the lined Pochita, and Jibbitz sold separately at $6.99 to $19.99 for Denji, Pochita, Aki, Power and Makima.\n\n![Chainsaw Man x Crocs via Complex](https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/c_crop,h_3207,w_4000,x_0,y_0/g_auto:aoi_1600_1284_800_641,ar_1.91,c_fill,q_auto,w_1200/sanity-new/nylnan3j5v0uqzwmmmm1 \"Complex / Crocs|https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/chainsaw-man-crocs-collection-release-date-footlocker\")\n\n## How to get it\n[Complex](https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/chainsaw-man-crocs-collection-release-date-footlocker) confirms Foot Locker is the exclusive retail partner. First access is Oct. 8 at New York Comic Con through a Chainsaw Man booth powered by Foot Locker, with a wider release at Footlocker.com and in stores \"later this fall.\" Oct. 27 has circulated as the retail date from secondary sites; Crocs hasn't confirmed it.\n\n## The context\nChainsaw Man's official account just confirmed the anime's next update comes at Jump Festa's Super Stage on Dec. 20 and 21, with the Assassins Arc confirmed and no format or date, per [ComicBook](https://comicbook.com/anime/news/chainsaw-man-confirms-next-major-anime-update-is-coming-soon/). So the clogs arrive in a gap: the Reze Arc film is a year old, and the next animated chapter is a December announcement at the earliest. Foot Locker, meanwhile, has been leaning into culture crossovers, including a brand platform narrated by Method Man this summer. A Javits Center booth with limited units is how you turn a convention line into a sell-out story.\n\n![Chainsaw Man x Crocs Pochita and Power clogs via CBR](https://static0.cbrimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/94619208-6f4f-428e-a311-d66edb43867f.jpg?w=1600&h=900&fit=crop \"CBR / Crocs|https://www.cbr.com/chainsaw-man-crocs-collection-foot-locker-nycc-release/\")\n\n## The read\nAnime footwear used to mean a Swoosh with a character on the heel. [What actually sold](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/anime-sneaker-collabs-history-adidas-dragon-ball-z-naruto-converse) was the stuff that committed to the bit. A clog with a chainsaw on it commits. For the hip-hop kids who grew up on Toonami and now wear Crocs to the function, this is the easiest $70 of the fall.\n\n## Sources\n- [Sneaker News, Sept. 29, 2026: Chainsaw Man's Crocs collaboration gets unhinged with an actual chainsaw attachment](https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/29/chainsaw-man-crocs-classic-clog/)\n- [Complex, Sept. 29, 2026: This Chainsaw Man x Crocs collection is releasing at Foot Locker](https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/chainsaw-man-crocs-collection-release-date-footlocker)\n- [CBR, Sept. 29, 2026: Chainsaw Man x Crocs collection, Foot Locker, NYCC release](https://www.cbr.com/chainsaw-man-crocs-collection-foot-locker-nycc-release/)\n- [ComicBook, Oct. 1, 2026: Chainsaw Man confirms next major anime update is coming soon](https://comicbook.com/anime/news/chainsaw-man-confirms-next-major-anime-update-is-coming-soon/)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
    "publishedAt": "2026-10-02",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-10-02"
