    "title": "The Game Sues UMG and Virgin Over Drillmatic's Budget",
    "headline": "The Game Sues Over\nDrillmatic's Budget",
    "subhead": "100 Entertainment says Virgin promised $500,000 to market the 2022 album and spent about $179,000, with nothing on radio. The suit, filed Sept. 30, says Game fronted costs that were then recouped from his own royalties.",
    "description": "The Game's 100 Entertainment sued UMG and Virgin Music for $500K on Sept. 30, alleging only $179K of a promised $500K Drillmatic marketing budget was spent.",
    "keywords": [
      "The Game",
      "The Game lawsuit",
      "UMG",
      "Virgin Music Group",
      "Drillmatic",
      "100 Entertainment",
      "Michael Trauben",
      "marketing budget",
      "Big Sean Stupid",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "THE GAME SUES OVER\nDRILLMATIC'S BUDGET",
    "ogAccent": "8B0000",
    "trendScore": 68,
    "heroCredit": "AceShowbiz",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.aceshowbiz.com/news/view/00262445.html",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "heroImage": "https://www.aceshowbiz.com/display/images/photo/2026/10/03/auto_00262445_1790979610.webp",
    "body": "Every artist who's been handed a marketing budget on paper has wondered where it went. The Game is asking a court.\n\n## The filing\nHis company, 100 Entertainment, sued Universal Music Group and Virgin Music Group in California Superior Court on Sept. 30, seeking $500,000, per [AceShowbiz](https://www.aceshowbiz.com/news/view/00262445.html) citing Billboard's report. The claim: the parties agreed to a $500,000 marketing budget for Drillmatic: Heart vs. Mind, the 30-track album Game released Aug. 12, 2022, and Virgin spent about $179,000 of it. Attorney Michael Trauben's complaint says nothing went to the $125,000 radio line and that key digital pieces were skipped; Digital Music News puts the shortfall at about $320,000.\n\n## Who paid for the rollout\nThe suit says 100 Entertainment covered marketing expenses out of pocket to keep the rollout on schedule, including the campaign for \"Stupid\" with Big Sean, and that UMG never reimbursed those costs. [Digital Music News](https://www.digitalmusicnews.com/2026/10/01/the-game-virgin-umg-lawsuit/) reports the complaint adds that the money Game fronted was later recouped from his royalties. Translation: he paid to market the label's release, then paid again.\n\n!youtube(https://youtu.be/8hBHOAJD3a0)\n\n## What the label says\nUMG and Virgin denied any breach in earlier communications with 100 Entertainment, per Billboard via AceShowbiz. Neither company had commented publicly on the lawsuit as of Friday. Drillmatic debuted at No. 12 with a first week of roughly 25,000 units, per Digital Music News, which the suit argues reflects an album \"deprived of nearly two-thirds\" of the support it was promised.\n\n![The Game \"Stupid\" ft. Big Sean via YouTube](https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8hBHOAJD3a0/maxresdefault.jpg \"The Game on YouTube|https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8hBHOAJD3a0\")\n\n## The read\nThis is the ownership story under every label deal. A \"budget\" in a distribution contract is a promise about someone else's money, and the artist usually can't audit it without a lawsuit. The $500,000 number is small by major-label standards. The discovery is the point: if the case gets to documents, every independent with a Virgin or UMG services deal will be reading them.\n\n## Sources\n- [AceShowbiz, Oct. 3, 2026: The Game sues UMG and Virgin Music for $500K over Drillmatic marketing](https://www.aceshowbiz.com/news/view/00262445.html)\n- [Digital Music News, Oct. 1, 2026: The Game sues Virgin and UMG](https://www.digitalmusicnews.com/2026/10/01/the-game-virgin-umg-lawsuit/)\n- [TMZ, Oct. 1, 2026: The Game's record label lawsuit](https://www.tmz.com/2026/10/01/the-game-record-label-lawsuit/)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
