    "heroImage": "https://www.jambase.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/doja-cat-latto-okayyy-detroit-v2-1480x832.jpg",
    "body": "The European leg was the warm-up. The American leg started Thursday in Detroit, and the opener didn't stay in her opening slot.\n\n## The moment\nLatto joined Doja Cat onstage at Little Caesars Arena on Oct. 1 for \"Okayyy,\" their track from Latto's fourth album Big Mama, per [JamBase](https://www.jambase.com/article/doja-cat-latto-okayyy-detroit-video-setlist). JamBase reports it was purportedly the first time the two performed the song together live. Latto is the support act for the whole North American run and did her own set before Doja's.\n\n!youtube(https://youtu.be/TTRCk8UROwU)\n\n## The set\nThirty-one songs, per the [setlist.fm data JamBase published](https://www.jambase.com/article/doja-cat-latto-okayyy-detroit-video-setlist): \"Cards,\" \"AAAHH MEN!,\" \"Kiss Me More,\" \"Get Into It (Yuh),\" \"Gorgeous,\" \"Take Me Dancing,\" \"Woman,\" \"Acts of Service,\" \"Agora Hills,\" \"Make It Up,\" \"Cyber Sex,\" \"You Right,\" \"All Mine,\" \"Shutcho,\" \"Ain't Shit,\" \"Paint the Town Red,\" \"Silly! Fun!,\" \"Okayyy,\" \"Juicy,\" \"97,\" \"Balut,\" \"Need to Know,\" \"Streets,\" \"Wet Vagina,\" \"WYM Freestyle,\" \"Demons,\" \"Tia Tamera,\" \"Boss Bitch,\" \"Stranger,\" \"One More Time,\" \"Say So,\" \"Jealous Type.\" That's the Vie material, the Scarlet songs, and the Hot Pink era, in one night.\n\n![Latto \"Okayyy\" ft. Doja Cat official video via YouTube](https://i.ytimg.com/vi/TTRCk8UROwU/maxresdefault.jpg \"Latto on YouTube|https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TTRCk8UROwU\")\n\n## Next\nChicago's United Center on Saturday, Oct. 3, then the run that ends Dec. 1 at Madison Square Garden. Both artists have rap credentials the pop charts keep trying to file elsewhere; Latto's Big Mama was one of the year's clearest rap-first records from a woman the industry markets as a crossover. Thirty-one songs and a Southern co-sign on night one is a statement about who this tour is for.\n\n## Sources\n- [JamBase, Oct. 2, 2026: Doja Cat and Latto link up at Detroit concert](https://www.jambase.com/article/doja-cat-latto-okayyy-detroit-video-setlist)\n- [Billboard, Oct. 2, 2026: Doja Cat setlist, Tour Ma Vie first U.S. show](https://www.billboard.com/lists/doja-cat-setlist-tour-ma-vie-songs-first-us-show/)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
