    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011501-kanye-russian-concerts-canceled-st-petersburg",
    "body": "The Russia shows are done. Say Agency confirmed Wednesday, Sept. 30, that Ye's St. Petersburg concerts planned for Oct. 10 and 11 are cancelled, per [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011501-kanye-russian-concerts-canceled-st-petersburg).\n\n## How it got here\nThe promoter announced the dates in August and said more than 100,000 tickets had been sold. That's the organizers' number, not an audited one. Gazprom Arena then said [there was never a lease agreement](https://theneedledrop.com/news/russian-stadium-cancels-kanye-west-concerts-there-was-and-is-no-lease-agreement/). In mid-September, [Meduza reported](https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/09/18/kanye-west-s-concerts-in-russia-removed-from-tour-schedule) the dates had been pulled from Ye's tour site. Say Agency kept sending conflicting messages for over a month before this week's confirmation.\n\n## The politics\nHotNewHipHop reports that Russian Foreign Ministry spokesperson Maria Zakharova opposed the concerts, citing Ye's history of antisemitic rhetoric and Nazi imagery. Officials also reportedly never signed off on the shows.\n\n## What fans do now\nTicket refunds are set to begin Oct. 12. That's also the date his civil trial is currently set for. We haven't seen a ruling on his request to push that trial, so don't read anything into the overlap beyond the calendar.\n\n## What's still on the calendar\nJakarta is Oct. 24, Houston is Halloween night, then Arlington and Phoenix in November. Those are the stadium dates still standing, and none of them have been reported as changed.\n\n## Sources\n- [HotNewHipHop: Ye's Russian concerts cancelled in St. Petersburg](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011501-kanye-russian-concerts-canceled-st-petersburg)\n- [Meduza: Ye's concerts in Russia removed from tour schedule](https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/09/18/kanye-west-s-concerts-in-russia-removed-from-tour-schedule)\n- [The Needle Drop: Russian stadium cancels Kanye West concerts](https://theneedledrop.com/news/russian-stadium-cancels-kanye-west-concerts-there-was-and-is-no-lease-agreement/)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
