    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011040-quavo-features-qromelife",
    "body": "QRÖMELIFE came out Friday, Oct. 2. It's 14 songs with Pharrell Williams guiding the project, according to [HotNewHipHop's rundown](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011040-quavo-features-qromelife).\n\n## Who's on it\nFuture on \"BA.\" Offset on \"Away.\" Lil Baby on \"Ball My Love.\" Yung Miami on \"HAOYU DEWDAT.\" Justin Timberlake on \"House Music.\" T.I. on \"Backwards.\" And \"Baby Breath\" has Tyler, The Creator, A$AP Rocky and Pharrell together.\n\n## What Quavo says it is\nHe described the album as a journey through tough times and out the other side, through faith, family and music. He credited Pharrell for pushing him creatively when he needed it.\n\n## The Migos part\nQuavo also said he's working on a separate project with Offset as a tribute to Takeoff. That's a stated plan, not a date. Nothing is announced yet beyond what he's said.\n\n## Where it sits this month\nOctober's calendar is thin until the 23rd. This is the first big Friday of the month, and we haven't reviewed it. Give it a full listen before you take a side. We'll add reactions once they exist.\n\n## Sources\n- [HotNewHipHop: Quavo reveals feature list on QRÖMELIFE](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011040-quavo-features-qromelife)\n- [Ratings Game Music: Quavo's QRÖMELIFE release date](https://ratingsgamemusic.com/2026/09/07/quavo-qrome-life-pharrell-album-october-2/)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
