    "body": "A big single-player action RPG with a firm date, a price and a studio saying the game is done. That's the whole pitch for Phantom Blade Zero, and it lands in under a month.\n\n## What's confirmed\nPhantom Blade Zero launches Oct. 29, 2026 on PlayStation 5 and PC. [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phantom_Blade_Zero) and [RPGamer](https://rpgamer.com/2026/08/phantom-blade-zero-pre-order-trailer-released/) both list Oct. 29, and RPGamer has PC on Steam and the Epic Games Store. [Push Square](https://www.pushsquare.com/news/2026/08/state-of-play-for-phantom-blade-zero-announced-for-next-week-11-minute-trailer-revealed) had pre-orders live on the PlayStation Store at $59.99, with a $69.99 Digital Deluxe that adds early outfit and accessory bonuses, a digital artbook and the soundtrack. One outlet, [Bleeding Cool](https://bleedingcool.com/games/phantom-blade-zero-releases-11-minute-video-as-pre-orders-start/), lists Oct. 28. That's almost certainly a time-zone difference, so go with the 29th and check your store page.\n\n## The delay, and the finish line\nThe game was first dated for Sept. 9. In June, per [RPG Site](https://www.rpgsite.net/news/20513-phantom-blade-zero-gets-new-special-teaser-trailer-at-june-2026-state-play), S-Game pushed it to Oct. 29 for more polish. [Gamereactor](https://www.gamereactor.eu/video/820953/Phantom+Blade+Zero+development+is+complete+and+the+game+is+ready+to+launch+in+late+October/) reported on Aug. 10 that development is complete and the game is ready for its late-October launch. A finished build with weeks to spare is what you want to hear after a delay.\n\n## What the 11-minute look showed\nPer RPGamer and Bleeding Cool, the extended video mixed story scenes and gameplay: you play Soul, an assassin on a 66-day clock after being framed for his master's murder, working through a world they call \"kungfupunk.\" Bleeding Cool lists more than 30 weapons and 20-plus \"Phantom Edges\" for combat. Donnie Yen is credited as creative consultant and did motion capture for the character Mó Yuan. Sony also scheduled a State of Play for Aug. 17 with almost 20 minutes of gameplay.\n\n## What's still open\nNo review scores exist yet, so nobody outside S-Game knows how the combat holds over 30 hours. Performance on base PS5 versus PC hasn't been publicly benchmarked. And Push Square describes the console version as PlayStation-exclusive while PC is confirmed elsewhere, so don't assume an Xbox version.\n\n## The cultural read\nA Beijing studio is getting the treatment the genre usually saves for western AAA: a State of Play slot, a delay to polish, a deluxe edition. Single-player RPG fans have spent the year being told nobody makes these anymore. This one is 25 days out, and it's finished.\n\n## Sources\n- [Wikipedia, Phantom Blade Zero](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phantom_Blade_Zero)\n- [Push Square, Aug. 12, 2026, State of Play and 11-minute trailer](https://www.pushsquare.com/news/2026/08/state-of-play-for-phantom-blade-zero-announced-for-next-week-11-minute-trailer-revealed)\n- [RPGamer, Aug. 12, 2026, pre-order trailer](https://rpgamer.com/2026/08/phantom-blade-zero-pre-order-trailer-released/)\n- [Gamereactor, Aug. 10, 2026, development complete](https://www.gamereactor.eu/video/820953/Phantom+Blade+Zero+development+is+complete+and+the+game+is+ready+to+launch+in+late+October/)\n- [RPG Site, June 2026, delay to Oct. 29](https://www.rpgsite.net/news/20513-phantom-blade-zero-gets-new-special-teaser-trailer-at-june-2026-state-play)\n- [Bleeding Cool, 11-minute video and pre-orders](https://bleedingcool.com/games/phantom-blade-zero-releases-11-minute-video-as-pre-orders-start/)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
