    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011657-eminem-kid-rock-7-sins-feature-backlash",
    "body": "Eminem and Kid Rock on the same song was always going to start an argument. This one started before most people have heard it.\n\n## What's reported\n[HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011657-eminem-kid-rock-7-sins-feature-backlash) reported on Oct. 1 that Eminem is featured on Kid Rock's \"7 Sins,\" and that the feature is stirring debate as fans look back at Eminem's 2017 anti-Trump ultimatum. That's the extent of what we could confirm. The report describes the track as upcoming. We found no release date, no statement from Eminem and no statement from Kid Rock.\n\n## The 2017 reference\nIn October 2017, Eminem used his [BET Hip Hop Awards cypher](https://www.complex.com/music/a/tracewilliamcowen/eminem-bet-cypher-trump-fan-reacts) to go after President Trump and told fans who supported Trump they'd have to pick a side. Kid Rock has been a public Trump supporter for years. That's why the new feature reads to some fans like a reversal. Others read it as one artist working with another, nothing more.\n\n## What nobody knows yet\nWhether \"7 Sins\" is a song about politics at all. Whether Eminem's verse touches the subject. When it drops. We haven't heard it, and a feature credit tells you who's on a record, not what it says.\n\n## The read\nFans hold artists to the lines they drew, especially when the line was drawn on a stage with a mic. Artists don't always see it that way. The only fair move is to wait for the song and the verse, then argue about what's on the record instead of the credit.\n\n## Sources\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 1, 2026, Eminem Kid Rock 7 Sins feature backlash](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011657-eminem-kid-rock-7-sins-feature-backlash)\n- [Complex, Eminem BET cypher and Trump fan reaction](https://www.complex.com/music/a/tracewilliamcowen/eminem-bet-cypher-trump-fan-reacts)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.",
