    "slug": "tay-roc-rum-nitty-name-flips-urltv-clip-summer-madness-xvi-october-3-2026",
    "pillar": "hiphop",
    "title": "Tay Roc's Name Flips on Rum Are the URL Clip of the Week",
    "headline": "Tay Roc Turned\n'Rum' Into a Weapon",
    "subhead": "URL posted Tay Roc's name flips on Rum Nitty from Summer Madness XVI. Here's what a name flip is, why the clip travels, and who owns the footage.",
    "description": "URL's Oct. 3 clip of Tay Roc flipping Rum Nitty's name from Summer Madness XVI is spreading. What a name flip is, why clips work, and who owns the full battle.",
    "keywords": [
      "Tay Roc",
      "Rum Nitty",
      "Summer Madness XVI",
      "URL",
      "URLtv",
      "battle rap",
      "name flips",
      "Smack",
      "Black-owned league",
      "hip-hop news",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "TAY ROC FLIPS\n'RUM' — URL CLIP",
    "ogAccent": "E0A100",
    "heroCredit": "Ultimate Rap League (URL) on X",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://x.com/urltv",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "trendScore": 74,
    "body": "Battle rap lives and dies on the timeline now. A forty-five second clip does more for a card than a month of announcements, and this week's clip is Tay Roc doing what he does to Rum Nitty's name.\n\n## What URL posted\nOn Oct. 3, the Ultimate Rap League account on X posted a clip from Summer Madness XVI praising Tay Roc's \"Rum\" name flips as insane. The post says the full event is out now on the URLtv app, with membership at $8.99 at URLtv.tv, and tags it #youcantcopyrespect. That's the whole post. It's a clip, a quote card and a paywall link in one tweet. Source: [@urltv on X](https://x.com/urltv).\n\nWe're not calling a winner off one clip, and we're not reading the bars. This one's explicit and it's a minute of an edited round. Watch the full battle.\n\n## What a name flip is\nA name flip takes your opponent's name and bends it into a punchline, a threat or a story. Done lazy, it's a pun. Done right, the name carries the whole verse and the crowd hears the word coming before the line lands. \"Rum\" is a short, loaded word, which gives a writer like Tay Roc plenty of angles. That's craft, and craft is why a clip gets quote-posted.\n\n## Who owns the footage\nSummer Madness is a URL event, and URL is a Black-owned league built by Tony \"Smack\" Mitchell, who turned a street-DVD hustle into a streaming business, per [Black Enterprise](https://blackenterprise.com/tony-smack-mitchell-urltv-battle-rap-smack/2). The model is simple. Free clips on social media pull people in, and the full rounds sit behind $8.99 a month. The league owns the footage and the distribution. We broke the whole stack down in [Battle Rap 301](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/battle-rap-301-smack-dvd-url-summer-madness-economics).\n\n## What's next\nTay Roc is also booked against Illmac in London on Oct. 25, per [our earlier report](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/tay-roc-vs-illmac-london-october-25-night-of-main-events-urltv-summer-madness-xvi-out-now-2026). We haven't seen a stream or card update.\n\n## The read\nClip on the timeline, tape behind the paywall. That's a Black-owned league running its own distribution, and the writers who make the clips go viral are the ones who should be asking about the cut. Watch the round, then pick your side.\n\n## Sources\n- [Ultimate Rap League (@urltv) on X, Oct. 3, 2026](https://x.com/urltv)\n- [Black Enterprise: Tony 'Smack' Mitchell on URLtv](https://blackenterprise.com/tony-smack-mitchell-urltv-battle-rap-smack/2)\n- [Sneakz & Beatz: Battle Rap 301](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/battle-rap-301-smack-dvd-url-summer-madness-economics)\n",
