    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "The new Sgt. Frog TV anime premiered October 3, 2026, and Anime News Network reports Crunchyroll is streaming it. It's the first new TV run for Keroro and the platoon since the original series ended after 358 episodes in 2011, per AniTrendz.\n\nIf you grew up on Cartoon Network-adjacent anime, Keroro was the weird little green frog trying to conquer Earth from a family basement. Low stakes, big heart. It hit different if you were a kid who wanted an alien invasion to be funny instead of scary.\n\n## What's new\n\nPer AniTrendz: BN Pictures is the studio, Akihiko Sano directs with Nobuhiko Kondo as chief director, and Hatsue Nakayama handles character design. The voice cast is all new. Makoto Koichi plays Keroro, Rika Nagae is Tamama, Toshiki Masuda is Giroro, Kosuke Echigoya is Kururu, and Satoshi Inomata is Dororo. ANN's earlier report said the old cast stays on the 20th anniversary film, while the TV series gets fresh voices.\n\nThe source manga started in 1999 in Shonen Ace and runs 35 volumes.\n\n## Why this one matters\n\nFall 2026 is stacked with sequels and big names. A reboot of a 2000s comfort show is the kind of thing that works because nostalgia and curiosity point the same way. Some people will watch for the memories. Some will watch to see if the new voices land.\n\nThe new cast is the real test. Voice casting is the whole personality of a comedy like this.\n\n## What we couldn't confirm\n\nWe couldn't pull the full ANN streaming article (the page returned an error), so regions, simulcast timing and dub plans are unconfirmed beyond the headline. Check Crunchyroll's listing for your country.\n\n## Sources\n- [Anime News Network, Crunchyroll Streams New Sgt. Frog TV Anime, October 3, 2026](https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-10-03/crunchyroll-streams-new-sgt-frog-tv-anime/.242453)\n- [AniTrendz, New Sgt. Frog TV Anime Drops Main Trailer and Key Visual, September 7, 2026](https://www.anitrendz.com/news/2026/09/07/new-sgt-frog-tv-anime-drops-main-trailer-and-key-visual-begins-on-october-3)\n- [Anime News Network, Sgt. Frog Manga Gets TV Anime With Brand-New Cast, December 23, 2025](https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-12-23/sgt-frog-manga-gets-tv-anime-with-brand-new-cast-next-fall/.232427)\n",
