    "heroCreditUrl": "https://dotesports.com/general/news/uncharted-new-game-naughty-dog",
    "trendScore": 72,
    "body": "Word is hitting the wires that Naughty Dog might be cooking up another Uncharted adventure. And for a brand that built its name on cinematic, high-stakes exploration, that kind of news lands differently than most.\n\n## The rumor\n\nMultiple outlets, including [Dot Esports](https://dotesports.com/general/news/uncharted-new-game-naughty-dog), [Push Square](https://pushsquare.com), and [Kotaku](https://kotaku.com), are reporting that a new Uncharted game is in development at Naughty Dog, following the studio's recent work on Intergalactic. The name floating around is Shaun Escayg, the director of The Last of Us Part II, who could be leading the project. As of now, Naughty Dog has not confirmed anything, and the whole thing remains unverified.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nUncharted isn't just a game. It's a cornerstone of modern adventure design. The series set the bar for how a third-person action game could feel like a blockbuster film, blending tight gunplay, fluid traversal, and a narrative that actually made you care about the people on screen. When a franchise like that goes quiet, the culture notices. A revival isn't just a new title on a release calendar; it's a statement about where Naughty Dog is placing its creative weight after years of pushing boundaries with The Last of Us.\n\n## The Shaun Escayg angle\n\nIf the report is accurate, putting Shaun Escayg at the helm is a bold move. He's known for a deeply emotional, character-driven take on storytelling, which could reshape Uncharted's identity. The original games leaned on charm, wit, and a sense of playful discovery. Escayg's style is heavier, more introspective. That tension could be the most interesting part of the story, even before a single frame of gameplay drops.\n\n## What we know and what we don't\n\nHere's the bottom line: this is a rumor. No official announcement. No trailer. No release window. What we have is cross-outlet chatter that a new Uncharted game is in the works, possibly under a new creative direction. Until Naughty Dog says otherwise, treat everything as unconfirmed. But the fact that the conversation is happening at all tells you something. The franchise still has weight, and the culture is ready for it to come back.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Dot Esports: New Uncharted Game Rumored at Naughty Dog](https://dotesports.com/general/news/uncharted-new-game-naughty-dog)\n- [Tech Insider: New Uncharted Game Rumor at Naughty Dog 2026](https://tech-insider.org/new-uncharted-game-rumor-naughty-dog-2026/)",
