    "body": "Offset has a date. His next album, GMFU, is set for Oct. 23, 17 days from now, and he said it himself.\n\n## What he posted\nPer [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1012004-offset-gmfu-new-album-release-date) on Oct. 4, Offset put the date in an Instagram caption on a Paris Fashion Week recap: album drop, Oct. 23. A follow-up Story explained the title, which is an abbreviation we're not spelling out here. HNHH also says he told Paper Magazine in a video that he's back to the music and ready to show what he's been working on.\n\n## What's missing\nThere's no tracklist, no feature list, no cover and no label announcement in the reporting we read. This is the artist's own post, not a formal rollout. Treat the date as his word until a pre-save or a cover shows up.\n\n## How it got here\nHNHH says Offset dropped the single \"Something I Need\" earlier this year. We covered [the hotline he opened ahead of it](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/offset-need-fm-hotline-something-i-need-single-september-18-migos-2026). Then came Quavo's QRÖMELIFE on Oct. 2, which includes \"Away,\" the first Quavo and Offset collaboration in five years. HNHH writes that the album didn't get a glowing reception, but that the moment mattered for the two of them.\n\n## The Migos part\nHNHH reports a Migos reunion is in the works to honor Takeoff, with new music and a tour. Quavo said on Oct. 1 that three Migos-related projects arrive in 2027, per HNHH. A strong Oct. 23 helps that story. A weak one makes it harder to sell.\n\n## The read\nQuavo went first. Offset's turn is 17 days out. Solo records are the proof of life before any group record, and everyone will be listening for quality, not nostalgia.\n\n## Sources\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 4, 2026: Offset reveals release date for new album](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1012004-offset-gmfu-new-album-release-date)\n- [HotNewHipHop: Offset tag](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/tag/offset)\n- [Sneakz & Beatz: Offset's hotline and \"Something I Need\"](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/offset-need-fm-hotline-something-i-need-single-september-18-migos-2026)\n",
