    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.complex.com/music/a/treyalston/travis-barker-goat-rapper-complexcon-2026",
    "trendScore": 66,
    "body": "Travis Barker was asked to name the greatest of all time at ComplexCon, and the drummer went West Coast first. His GOAT album is Dr. Dre's *The Chronic*.\n\n![Travis Barker at ComplexCon 2026](https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/c_crop,h_1802,w_3382,x_0,y_0/g_auto:aoi_1353_721_676_360,ar_1.91,c_fill,q_auto,w_1200/sanity-new/f1twtw91vu1hgth42rqu \"Complex|https://www.complex.com/music/a/treyalston/travis-barker-goat-rapper-complexcon-2026\")\n\n## The picks\nPer [Complex's GOAT Talk with Barker](https://www.complex.com/music/a/treyalston/travis-barker-goat-rapper-complexcon-2026), published Oct. 4 from ComplexCon 2026, the Blink-182 drummer didn't hesitate on the album. \"I'm from the West Coast,\" he said. \"West Coast rap raised me.\"\n\nHis GOAT rappers came in a short stack: Jay-Z, Kendrick Lamar and Lil Wayne. On Hov, Barker said, \"Jay-Z is undeniable. You know his discography. His history.\"\n\n## Why it lands\nBarker has been in rap rooms for two decades, as a producer, a session drummer and a live-band engine behind artists who wanted rock energy under their bars. So his list reads like a man who has watched the work up close, not a fan quoting a poll. Dre's *The Chronic* is the foundation of the sound he grew up on. Jay-Z is the catalog. Kendrick is the current standard. Wayne is the run that rewired the mixtape era.\n\nIt also comes the same weekend ComplexCon turned into a rap story from every angle, with Playboi Carti and Ken Carson headlining, Ye on the floor and the Lucki fight dominating the timeline. Barker's answers were the calm one.\n\n## The read\nGOAT lists are bait, and every one starts an argument. This one is hard to fight, because the names are earned. Drop your own top three below, and tell us who Barker left off.\n\n## Sources\n- [Complex, Oct. 4, 2026: Travis Barker Runs Through His GOAT Rappers, Albums and More at ComplexCon](https://www.complex.com/music/a/treyalston/travis-barker-goat-rapper-complexcon-2026)\n",
