    "trendScore": 58,
    "body": "Gran Turismo 7 is getting a free update next week, and it's a big one for the garage. Spec IV Part 1 lands Oct. 14 at 11 p.m. PT on PS4 and PS5.\n\n![Gran Turismo 7 Spec IV Part 1 key art](https://gamingbolt.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Gran-Turismo-7-October-Update-scaled.jpg \"GamingBolt|https://gamingbolt.com/gran-turismo-7-spec-iv-part-1-launches-on-october-14th-adds-6-new-vehicles-and-sugo-racing-course\")\n\n## What's in it\nPer [GamingBolt](https://gamingbolt.com/gran-turismo-7-spec-iv-part-1-launches-on-october-14th-adds-6-new-vehicles-and-sugo-racing-course), Part 1 adds six cars: the Honda Civic SI Group A 1987, Honda Step WGN Spada Premium Line 2023, Citroën 2CV 6 Charleston 1986, Ferrari F355 Berlinetta 1994, Mazda RX-Vision GT3 EVO 2026 and the Xiaomi Vision Gran Turismo. It also brings SUGO International Racing Course.\n\n!youtube(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0_7kHG8Hpx8)\n\nThe update also adds a Car Concierge for ordering Used and Legend cars, a Car Viewer for inspecting your garage, brand-specific challenges in Experience mode and a new opening cinematic.\n\n## What's next\nPart 2 follows in December with more cars, the Autumn Ring circuit, a Family mode and online drift racing. [Traxion](https://traxion.gg/?p=107669) counts 12 new cars across both parts, with the December list still not fully announced. Traxion lists the October date as Oct. 15, which matches the 11 p.m. PT Oct. 14 timing in other time zones.\n\n## The read\nFree content is the whole pitch here. Gran Turismo has been a car-culture staple for the PlayStation generation, and a Ferrari, a JDM wagon and a Xiaomi concept in one drop is the usual GT range. Update your garage early.\n\n## Sources\n- [GamingBolt, Oct. 4, 2026: Gran Turismo 7 Spec IV Part 1 Launches on October 14th](https://gamingbolt.com/gran-turismo-7-spec-iv-part-1-launches-on-october-14th-adds-6-new-vehicles-and-sugo-racing-course)\n- [Traxion, Oct. 2026: Gran Turismo 7 Spec IV cars](https://traxion.gg/?p=107669)\n",
