    "goLiveAt": "2026-10-09",
    "body": "Offset gave the album a date on Instagram. Now he's given it a song.\n\n## What dropped\n\"Every Night,\" with Don Toliver, hit Oct. 8. [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1012419-every-night-offset-don-toliver) lists it as a single from GMFU, the album Offset dated for Oct. 23. That's 14 days from today. We're saying the letters, G-M-F-U, because the spelled-out title is explicit.\n\n## What's missing\nNo tracklist in the reporting we read. No cover, no label statement, no full feature list. The date and title come from Offset's own posts, so call it his date.\n\n## Why Don Toliver\nIt's a smart pairing for a first look. Toliver's melodic lane gives Offset room to sing rather than stack ad-libs. We haven't broken the record down line by line, and we're not going to guess at the sound for you. Press play and judge it yourself.\n\n## The bigger picture\nQuavo's QRÖMELIFE landed first. Offset's run is shaping up as the second chapter of a family story fans keep watching. [HNHH has framed](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/tag/offset) a Migos reunion as the long game. The solo records are the proof of life.\n\n## Sources\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 8, 2026: \"Every Night\" by Offset and Don Toliver](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1012419-every-night-offset-don-toliver)\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 4, 2026: Offset reveals release date for GMFU](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1012004-offset-gmfu-new-album-release-date)"
