    "body": "URL posted the card Thursday, and it just got heavier.\n\n## The announcement\nPer [@urltv on X](https://x.com/urltv): Dizaster vs. Rum Nitty, London, England, Oct. 25, Night of Main Events. Tickets are on sale now through thesteelyard.london. That's 16 days out.\n\n## Same night as Tay Roc vs. Illmac\nWe already know the card carries [Tay Roc vs. Illmac](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/tay-roc-vs-illmac-london-october-25-night-of-main-events-urltv-summer-madness-xvi-out-now-2026). Two headline-level matchups on one London night. That's a statement from a Black-owned league.\n\n## Why this one\nRum Nitty just came off Summer Madness XVI in Atlanta against Tay Roc. The fan vote went 2-1 Tay Roc, with Rum taking Round 1, and URL has been clipping his antonym and synonym scheme all week. Dizaster is a veteran who's been in the biggest rooms for years. A scheme-heavy writer against a pure performer makes for a real style clash.\n\n## What we don't have\nNo odds, no rules, no confirmed undercard in what we saw. The announcement is one post. We haven't seen a statement from either battler. We're not calling a winner, because nobody's stepped on the stage.\n\n## The read\nClip the best rounds, buy the card, then argue. That's how this culture feeds itself.\n\n## Sources\n- [@urltv on X, Oct. 8, 2026: Dizaster vs. Rum Nitty, London, Oct. 25](https://x.com/urltv)\n- [Sneakz & Beatz: Tay Roc vs. Illmac, London, Oct. 25](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/tay-roc-vs-illmac-london-october-25-night-of-main-events-urltv-summer-madness-xvi-out-now-2026)"
