    "goLiveAt": "2026-10-09",
    "body": "Rockstar opened the radio. If you've been waiting to hear what Leonida sounds like, you can preview it now.\n\n## The stations\nPer [Push Square's report](https://www.pushsquare.com/news/2026/10/gta-6-in-game-radio-stations-announced-and-you-can-preview-them-right-now) on the Rockstar Newswire post, six stations are named. Cocoteo FM (Latin), Back Country Radio (country), AfroBank FM (African), The Chamber 106.6 (metal), Flash FM (pop) and Dirty South Classics (Southern rap and hip-hop), hosted by Trick and Trina. Those are some of the stations, not all. On-demand podcasts are in too, a first for the series.\n\n## The hip-hop part\nDirty South Classics previews include David Banner with Lil' Flip and JT Money with Solé, plus a DJ Khaled record with Trick Daddy. A Southern rap station run by two Southern rap veterans fits the Miami setting. Other previews include Bad Bunny, Asake, Black Sabbath, Pantera, Charli xcx and Loretta Lynn. That's range.\n\n## Release\nGTA VI is dated Nov. 19, 2026. That's 41 days out. Previews are on Rockstar's music page.\n\n## The read\nRadio is how this series tells you where it is. Southern rap on Trick and Trina's mic says Rockstar knows the region it's playing in.\n\n## Sources\n- [Push Square, Oct. 8, 2026: GTA 6 in-game radio stations announced](https://www.pushsquare.com/news/2026/10/gta-6-in-game-radio-stations-announced-and-you-can-preview-them-right-now)\n- [Rockstar Games Newswire](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire)"
