    "heroFocus": "center",
    "trendScore": 68,
    "publishedAt": "2026-10-09",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-10-09",
    "body": "No Cyberpunk patch this week. But a CD Projekt Red developer talked, and the game came up.\n\n## The interview\n[RPG Site](https://www.rpgsite.net/interview/21527-the-witcher-3-remastered-switch-2-interview-cd-projekt-red-oleg-shatulo-cross-save-dlss-ps5-pro-new) spoke with Oleg Shatulo, who works on the Cyberpunk 2077 Nintendo Switch 2 and Mac initiatives and on updates for the game. The Oct. 8 piece is mostly about Witcher 3 Remastered.\n\n## What carried over\nShatulo says the Cyberpunk Switch 2 work gave the team experience with DLSS on that hardware, which they applied to Witcher 3. The article says the two games still needed separate tuning.\n\n## What he didn't say\nNo Cyberpunk update details. No dates. No word on what the \"updates\" are. Everything here is the developer's own description of his role.\n\n## Witcher 3 side note\nPer the same interview, saves carry forward into the remaster, not back. Moving a save from the original Switch version needs a CD PROJEKT RED account and doesn't happen automatically.\n\n## The read\nCyberpunk is still being worked on, and the work is feeding the studio's next big port. With Edgerunners 2 arriving Oct. 20, a quiet game is fine. The anime is the front door.\n\n## Sources\n- [RPG Site, Oct. 8, 2026: The Witcher 3 Remastered Switch 2 interview](https://www.rpgsite.net/interview/21527-the-witcher-3-remastered-switch-2-interview-cd-projekt-red-oleg-shatulo-cross-save-dlss-ps5-pro-new)"
