    "heroCredit": "Ultimate Rap League on X",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://x.com/urltv",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "trendScore": 78,
    "body": "URL doesn't let the room cool off. Less than two weeks after Summer Madness XVI wrapped, the league stacked a London card.\n\n## The card so far\nPer [Ultimate Rap League's posts on X](https://x.com/urltv), Night of Main Events 16 is set for London, Oct. 25. On Oct. 7 URL posted Tay Roc vs. Illmac and Calicoe vs. T-Top. On Oct. 8 it added Dizaster vs. Rum Nitty. Tickets are on sale through thesteelyard.london, according to URL's own posts. That's three confirmed matchups, and it's not necessarily the full card.\n\n## Why Rum Nitty vs. Dizaster\nRum Nitty just came out of Atlanta with a fan-vote loss to Tay Roc that still had people talking, because he took Round 1 in the same poll. Now he's booked against Dizaster, one of the most recognizable names in the culture. URL keeps handing its biggest names a next date before the last one fades.\n\n## Tay Roc vs. Illmac\nWe covered [the first announcement](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/tay-roc-vs-illmac-london-october-25-night-of-main-events-urltv-summer-madness-xvi-out-now-2026). The update is the label and the on-sale date: URL now bills it as part of NOME 16 with tickets live. Tay Roc fought Sept. 27 in Atlanta. He's back on a stage 28 days later.\n\n## What isn't confirmed\nWe haven't seen a full card, a stream plan, a pay-per-view price or a venue name from URL. If a streaming option exists, it hasn't been posted where we looked. Check the league's page before you plan around it.\n\n## The read\nThis is a Black-owned league building a London night around its own stars, on its own calendar. Nobody handed it a platform. Fifteen days out, three matchups are set. Watch the posts for the rest.\n\n## Sources\n- [Ultimate Rap League on X, Oct. 7-8, 2026: NOME 16 matchups](https://x.com/urltv)\n- [Sneakz and Beatz: Tay Roc vs Illmac heads to London](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/tay-roc-vs-illmac-london-october-25-night-of-main-events-urltv-summer-madness-xvi-out-now-2026)\n",
