    "ogHeadline": "lola gets her\nown jordan 3.",
    "ogAccent": "E87AA6",
    "trendScore": 70,
    "body": "The Air Jordan 3 \"Lola Bunny\" is a girls' release, and it's the first Jordan 3 in the Space Jam 30th anniversary run. Reported date is November 5, 2026. Reported price is $155 under style code IZ1694-600. Jordan Brand hasn't confirmed any of it yet, so treat the details as a strong first look, not gospel.\n\n## What's reported\n\nWhite leather base. Light pink overlays, hot pink contrast stitching, royal blue interior. A translucent blush-pink outsole sits under a white midsole with a visible Air unit. The left tongue carries a new pink Lola Bunny Jumpman. The right tongue keeps the yellow one. Both [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/07/air-jordan-3-lola-bunny-iz1694-600/) and [JustFreshKicks](https://justfreshkicks.com/?p=243649) describe a tan pom-pom hangtag built like a bunny tail, speckled royal blue laces, and an extra set of fuzzy laces in the box.\n\nSmall stuff, but it's where the pair earns its keep: Lola dunking on the insoles, and a Lola-themed box with a pink lid. JustFreshKicks also notes an iridescent orange, pink, and blue gradient on the heel tabs. Sneaker News doesn't mention that detail, so I'm holding it as single-source.\n\n## The part worth talking about\n\nSneaker News describes this as a Grade School release designed for girls. Neither outlet lists a size run, and I couldn't confirm women's sizing. That's the question that decides who actually gets to buy it. Lola Bunny was the 1996 movie's answer to a basketball world that mostly had room for one lead. She got a character. Thirty years later she gets her own Jordan 3, and the only open question is whether the grown women who grew up on that movie can buy it or only their kids can.\n\nKids' exclusives have a habit of getting scooped by adults in sizes that don't fit anyone. That's a pattern, not a prediction for this pair. If Nike wants the anniversary to land with the people who actually watched Space Jam in theaters, a women's run is the move. Watch the SKU listings as the date gets closer.\n\n## Where it sits\n\nPart of the Space Jam 30th anniversary lineup, alongside the Air Jordan 11 pairs. If you want the full collection and dates, start with our breakdown of the [Air Jordan 11 Space Jam 30th anniversary collection](/the-lane/air-jordan-11-space-jam-30th-anniversary-collection-december-12-green-screen-magic-ball-november-2026). The Jordan 3 \"Lola Bunny\" release date is listed for Thursday, November 5, at Nike and Jordan retailers.\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated from San Diego. Run by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming.\n\n## Sources\n- [Sneaker News, Oct. 7, 2026 (updated Oct. 8)](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/07/air-jordan-3-lola-bunny-iz1694-600/)\n- [JustFreshKicks, Oct. 7, 2026](https://justfreshkicks.com/?p=243649)\n- [SneakerFiles Air Jordan release dates, accessed Oct. 9, 2026](https://www.sneakerfiles.com/air-jordan-release-dates/)\n",
