    "body": "The October PlayStation Plus Game Catalog is nine games, and most land Tuesday, October 20. Insider Gaming published the list October 14. If you're on Extra or Premium, here's what's coming.\n\n## Extra and Premium\n\n- **The Midnight Walk** (PS5) — October 15\n- **Mafia: The Old Country** (PS5) — October 20\n- **Horizon Forbidden West** (PS5, PS4, re-release) — October 20\n- **Mycopunk** (PS5, day-one launch) — October 20\n- **Poppy Playtime: Chapter 2** (PS5, PS4) — October 27\n- **Tales of Arise – Beyond the Dawn Edition** (PS5, PS4) — October 27\n- **Monster Energy Supercross 25** (PS5) — October 27\n\n## Premium only\n\n**Dino Crisis 2** and **Roller Coaster Tycoon 3 Complete Edition** (both PS5, PS4). Insider Gaming says most games arrive Oct. 20 unless noted and doesn't give these two a separate date, so we're treating them as Oct. 20 and flagging it.\n\n## The take\n\nMafia: The Old Country on a subscription is the pull. Period crime story, big production, no $70 ask. Horizon Forbidden West is the safe pick if you skipped it. And a day-one launch for Mycopunk on the catalog is the kind of move that tells you where Sony's subscription is headed.\n\nAlready on the October monthly games? That's F1 25, Hunt: Showdown 1896 and Earth Defense Force: World Brothers 2, per the PlayStation Blog, live until November 2. Details in [our monthly games rundown](/the-lane/playstation-plus-october-2026-f1-25-hunt-showdown-1896-earth-defense-force-world-brothers-2).\n\n## Unverified\n\nLineups can differ by region. We did not confirm this list against PlayStation's own catalog post, so check the PlayStation Store on the day.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Insider Gaming — PlayStation Plus Games Catalog adds 9 games in October 2026 (Oct. 14, 2026)](https://insider-gaming.com/playstation-plus-games-catalog-adds-9-games-in-october-2026/)\n- [PlayStation Blog — PlayStation Plus Monthly Games for October (Sept. 30, 2026)](https://blog.playstation.com/2026/09/30/playstation-plus-monthly-games-for-october-f1-25-hunt-showdown-1896-earth-defense-force-world-brothers-2/)\n",
