    "body": "Quavo laid out the next stretch of his catalog in one radio sit-down, and none of it has a date yet.\n\nSpeaking with Justin Credible on Power 106 in Los Angeles, he said another solo album is coming behind *QRÖMELIFE* (out Oct. 2): \"I got another album coming right after.\" On the group: \"Of course, we going to cook up the Migos project.\" And on his late nephew: \"we working on Take project, too.\" That is the account in [XXL's Oct. 13 report](https://www.xxlmag.com/quavo-new-music-migos-album-takeoff-project/), which also points to an earlier talk with V-103's DJ Greg Street where he discussed touring for the planned Migos and Takeoff records.\n\n## What is confirmed and what is not\nConfirmed, by Quavo's own words: three projects exist in some form. Not confirmed: titles, release windows, tracklists, or who is on them. Whether Offset is part of the Migos record is not addressed in the XXL piece. Our earlier read on that thread: [Migos' final album and the Quavo/Offset question](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/migos-final-album-tour-quavo-offset-2026). Treat the Takeoff LP especially as in-progress, since nothing beyond Quavo's statement has been reported.\n\n## Why it matters\nTakeoff's music is the one the culture is waiting on, and how it is handled (who gets paid, who curates, what the estate signs off on) is the real story when it arrives. A Migos project without a settled lineup is a business question before it is a music question. Right now the only firm fact is that Quavo is saying all three out loud, on the radio, in the same week.\n\n## Sources\n- [XXL - Quavo Confirms More Solo Music, a Migos Album and Takeoff Project (Oct. 13, 2026)](https://www.xxlmag.com/quavo-new-music-migos-album-takeoff-project/)\n- [Sneakz & Beatz - Migos' final album, tour and the Quavo/Offset question](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/migos-final-album-tour-quavo-offset-2026)\n",
    "publishedAt": "2026-10-14T21:30:00-07:00",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-10-15"
