    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "*Warhammer Survivors* launches November 10 on PS5, per a [PlayStation Blog post](https://blog.playstation.com/2026/10/06/warhammer-survivors-launches-november-10-new-characters-revealed/) dated October 6, 2026 and written by designer Ellie Harrodine of developer Auroch Digital. Wishlisting and pre-orders opened with that post, and PlayStation Plus members get 10% off pre-orders.\n\n## The champions\n\nTwo characters were revealed. Morvenn Vahl is an Adepta Sororitas commander who fights in a Paragon Warsuit with the Heavy Bolter Fidelis. Lyssa Revenya is a thief from the Saviours of Cinderfall who uses a Rope and Grapnel. The game has more than 40 playable champions in total.\n\n## What it is\n\nThe name tells you the genre: you're a survivor in a horde, building a loadout and fighting through waves. It takes that formula into the Warhammer universe, and Auroch Digital is leaning on character variety to separate it from the pack. Forty-plus champions is a lot of builds to try.\n\n## The take\n\nLook, the horde-survival lane is crowded, and Warhammer's grim-dark art direction is a real hook. A big roster only matters if each champion plays differently. The two shown here do look distinct. I'd wait on reviews before spending, but I'm interested.\n\n## Unconfirmed\n\nThe PlayStation Blog post doesn't list a price, and it doesn't state the year in the body text (the post itself is dated October 6, 2026). Check the PlayStation Store listing for the price.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [PlayStation Blog — Warhammer Survivors launches November 10, new characters revealed (Oct. 6, 2026)](https://blog.playstation.com/2026/10/06/warhammer-survivors-launches-november-10-new-characters-revealed/)",
