    "heroCreditUrl": "https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/07/air-jordan-1-space-jam-2026/",
    "body": "The Air Jordan 1 \"Space Jam\" is real, and it's coming in two heights. Per [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/07/air-jordan-1-space-jam-2026/), the Air Jordan 1 Mid (IX6374-001) is $140 and the Air Jordan 1 Low (IX6375-001) is $130, both listed for November 2026. Grade school sizes run $120 and $115.\n\n## What's on the shoe\nThe Mid carries concentric circles on the Swoosh, with planet-like rings near the curved edges. Sneaker News compares the look to the Joker's palette. The Low goes metallic: iridescent finishes break the panels into multicolor, and Sneaker News ties it to the Air Jordan 11 \"Magic Blue.\" Both come in a special box with movie call-outs and 30th anniversary branding, with the Jumpman leaping through an orbital diagram.\n\nTwo more pairs were added in an update: a women's Air Jordan 1 Low SE (IX6038-100, $130) with iridescent overlays and mismatched \"Air Jordan\" heel branding, and a second Mid (IZ9293-001, $140) with a sportier look that hints at classic Bugs Bunny colors.\n\n## The date, and what's not confirmed\nSneaker News lists everything as \"Coming Soon\" for November. A separate Sneaker News [collection rundown](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/08/jordan-11-space-jam/) puts the Air Jordan 1 Low and Mid in a Nov. 5 wave, but it doesn't give the 1s a price, so we're treating Nov. 5 as the working date, not a lock. Retail listings are thin: the first two list Nikestore only, and the IZ9293-001 Mid lists Nikestore, Finish Line, Foot Locker, Champs and DICK'S.\n\n## Why it matters\nThis is a 30th anniversary run for a movie that sold a whole generation on Jordan, and Jordan Brand is spreading it across the catalog: an Air Jordan 9, three Air Jordan 11 looks, and now the 1. We already tracked the [Air Jordan 9 Space Jam](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-9-og-space-jam-2026-tune-squad) and the [Air Jordan 11 collection](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-11-space-jam-30th-anniversary-collection-december-12-green-screen-magic-ball-november-2026). The 1 is the cheap way in.\n\n## The take\nThe 11s are the shoes people will fight over. The 1 Mid at $140 is the one you can actually wear to the grocery store without losing sleep. If you're after one pair from this run, the price gap is the story.\n\n## Sources\n- Sneaker News, Oct. 7, 2026: [Air Jordan 1 \"Space Jam\" 2026](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/07/air-jordan-1-space-jam-2026/)\n- Sneaker News, Oct. 8, 2026: [Jordan Brand Expands The Space Jam Universe With A Massive Collection](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/08/jordan-11-space-jam/)\n\nBuilt for the culture. Operated by PHRHX through Sneakz & Beatz LLC. Black-owned, four pillars: sneakers, hip-hop, anime, gaming."
