    "trendScore": 74,
    "body": "On October 3 we told you to reset your reminders to December 18. Pull the reset back. [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/12/apb-air-jordan-11-low-made-for-locals-iu8266-400/), [Complex](https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/apb-air-jordan-11-made-for-locals-everything-you-need-to-know) and [Sole Retriever](https://www.soleretriever.com/news/articles/apb-x-air-jordan-11-low-made-for-local-release-details-october-2026) all now list the APB x Air Jordan 11 Low \"Made for Locals\" for Friday, October 23, and raffles are open.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe December date came from [HotNewHipHop on October 3](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011949-apb-x-air-jordan-11-low-binary-blue-sneaker-news-2), which had the shoe sliding from September 18 to December 18. We [covered that move](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/apb-air-jordan-11-low-binary-blue-delayed-december-18-200-hotnewhiphop-2026) and said a date that moved once could move again. It did. None of the three outlets explains the reversal, and none mentions the December report. We can't tell you why. Treat October 23 as the working date and wait for the retailer confirmation on drop day.\n\n## The shoe\n\nStyle code IU8266-400, $200. Sneaker News describes Binary Blue patent leather on the mudguard and matte leather on the upper panels, with Rust Pink piping running 360 degrees around the upper. Sole Retriever adds an icy blue outsole and salmon pink accents on the sockliner. It is the same pair we first covered as [\"Binary Blue\" in September](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/apb-air-jordan-11-low-binary-blue-iu8266-400-september-18-whitaker-group-2026), now with a name.\n\n![APB x Air Jordan 11 Low \"Made for Locals\" detail](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/apb-air-jordan-11-low-made-for-locals-IU8266-400-1.jpg \"Sneaker News|https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/12/apb-air-jordan-11-low-made-for-locals-iu8266-400/\")\n\n## Made for locals\n\nSneaker News says the name is an ode to the neighborhood spots, the deli, the coffee shop, the sneaker store. Sole Retriever reports APB is the skate shop arm of The Whitaker Group and that the launch campaign has locals picking up the pair, with footage of the crew skating in the patent leather 11s. Complex quotes the label calling the shoe a tribute to \"the people, gathering places and everyday experiences that give neighborhoods their identity.\"\n\n## Where and how\n\nThe drop runs at Whitaker Group retailers: APB, [A Ma Maniere](https://www.a-ma-maniere.com), JAIDE and Social Status. Sneaker News says all four have EQL raffles. Complex lists a separate APB Instagram giveaway with a winner announced October 20. Price is $200 per Sneaker News and Sole Retriever.\n\n## The read\n\nThe 11 is Jordan Brand's December shoe, and a collab on the Low is rare. Putting it in a skate shop's hands, in October, with the neighbors in the campaign, is a Whitaker Group move: Black-owned retail telling the story of the block the shoe is sold on. If the date holds, the people it was made for get it first.\n\nRelated: [Air Jordan release dates this week](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-release-dates-this-week-october-19-25-2026-apb-11-low-aj12-fireside-aj1-halloween-dia-de-muertos).\n\n## Sources\n- [Sneaker News, Oct. 12, 2026: APB x Air Jordan 11 Low \"Made For Locals\"](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/12/apb-air-jordan-11-low-made-for-locals-iu8266-400/)\n- [Complex, Oct. 12, 2026: APB Air Jordan 11 \"Made for Locals,\" everything you need to know](https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/apb-air-jordan-11-made-for-locals-everything-you-need-to-know)\n- [Sole Retriever, Oct. 13, 2026: APB x Air Jordan 11 Low \"Made for Locals\" release details](https://www.soleretriever.com/news/articles/apb-x-air-jordan-11-low-made-for-local-release-details-october-2026)\n- [HotNewHipHop, Oct. 3, 2026: \"Binary Blue\" pushed back to December](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1011949-apb-x-air-jordan-11-low-binary-blue-sneaker-news-2)\n",
