    "ogHeadline": "JORDAN RELEASE WEEK:\nFOUR PAIRS, TWO DAYS.",
    "ogAccent": "C8102E",
    "heroImage": "https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/air-jordan-12-fireside-CT8013-105-6.jpg",
    "heroCredit": "Sneaker News",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/09/air-jordan-12-fireside-ct8013-105/",
    "trendScore": 71,
    "body": "The Air Jordan 5 \"Halloween\" came out Saturday. This week is smaller on volume and bigger on range: a collab 11 Low on Friday, then a seasonal 12 and two Air Jordan 1s on Saturday. Dates and prices below are from [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/air-jordan-release-dates/) and [SneakerFiles](https://www.sneakerfiles.com/air-jordan-release-dates/). Where they disagree on price, both numbers are shown.\n\n## Friday, October 23\n\n**APB x Air Jordan 11 Low \"Made for Locals\" (IU8266-400), $200.** The Whitaker Group skate shop's first Jordan, back on after a December report. Raffles run through APB, A Ma Maniere, JAIDE and Social Status. Full breakdown: [APB's Jordan 11 Low is back on](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/apb-air-jordan-11-low-made-for-locals-october-23-back-from-december-iu8266-400-2026).\n\n## Saturday, October 24\n\n**Air Jordan 12 \"Fireside\" (CT8013-105).** Log Brown and Off Noir with Nike Air. Sneaker News lists $220 for adults; SneakerFiles lists $215. Grade school, little kids and infant sizes run alongside. Our [official look](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-12-fireside-ct8013-105-october-24-official-look-2026) has the details.\n\n**Air Jordan 1 Low \"Halloween\" (IQ5494-001).** Black with Scream Green and Dark Smoke Grey. SneakerFiles lists $130 and our earlier [official images](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-1-low-halloween-black-neon-green-glow-iq5494-001-official-images-2026) piece had $125, so confirm the number at checkout.\n\n**Air Jordan 1 Mid \"Dia de Los Muertos\" (IZ4718-283), $145.** The U.S. release of the pair we covered in the [official images](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-1-mid-dia-de-muertos-iz4718-283-official-images-xolo-en-esta-familia-october-2026). Not to be confused with the Mexico-only [AJ1 Low OG \"Somos Historias\"](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-1-low-og-somos-historias-iz4686-216-5026-pairs-dia-de-los-muertos-mexico-october-13-2026).\n\n## Behind them\n\nHalloween weekend is already stacked. The women's Air Jordan 3 \"Fireside\" (CK9246-200) is listed for October 30 at $205, and the Air Jordan 14 \"Forest Green\" (487471-300) for Saturday, October 31 at $215, the [first retro of that colorway since 2005](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-14-forest-green-2026-release-date-price). SneakerFiles also lists an Air Jordan 4 \"Light Army\" (JA5911-320) for October 31 at $220; we previously reported that pair as a [Europe exclusive](https://www.sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-4-light-army-ja5911-320-europe-exclusive-october-2-2026), so check the region before you plan around it.\n\n## The read\n\nThree of the four pairs this week are seasonal colorways or collabs, not heritage retros. That is the strategy: keep the Jordan calendar full of lower-stakes releases so the Space Jam and Bred 4 weeks in November carry the weight. Pick the one you would wear, not the one a resale sheet tells you to flip.\n\n## Sources\n- [Sneaker News, Air Jordan release dates (accessed Oct. 18, 2026)](https://sneakernews.com/air-jordan-release-dates/)\n- [SneakerFiles, Air Jordan release dates (accessed Oct. 18, 2026)](https://www.sneakerfiles.com/air-jordan-release-dates/)\n- [Sneaker News, Oct. 12, 2026: APB x Air Jordan 11 Low \"Made For Locals\"](https://sneakernews.com/2026/10/12/apb-air-jordan-11-low-made-for-locals-iu8266-400/)\n",
