      "heroCreditUrl": "https://ratingsgamemusic.com/2026/10/16/meek-mill-g-herbo-wanna-be-free-review/",
      "body": "Meek Mill and G Herbo put out \"Wanna Be Free\" on October 16, 2026, per [Baller Alert's New Music Friday roundup](https://balleralert.com/o2og). It's a single of roughly five minutes through DreamChasers, distributed by Stem, and it follows Meek's July single \"Nightmares To Dreams.\" Whether it belongs to an album or project hasn't been stated in anything I found.\n\n## What's on it\n\n[Ratings Game Music](https://ratingsgamemusic.com/2026/10/16/meek-mill-g-herbo-wanna-be-free-review/) paraphrases it as two rappers looking back at rough come-ups while talking about the lives they live now, and says that contrast gives the flexing context. It scored the song 3.5 out of 5. Baller Alert says G Herbo's angle is that money doesn't erase your past. Production wasn't credited in either source.\n\n## Why it's worth a listen\n\nMeek and Herbo have history on record. The two paired up before on \"Survivor's Guilt\" in May 2025, per [Ratings Game Music](https://ratingsgamemusic.com/2025/05/30/meek-mill-g-herbo-survivors-guilt-review). Philly and Chicago both come out of environments where success and survivor's guilt arrive together. That's the lane they're working in again.\n\n## The take\n\nReal talk, it's a good week for Meek to put out something serious. He's been in the headlines for [stadium-sized sell-out talk](/the-lane/meek-mill-says-he-can-sell-out-msg-barclays-45-days-akademiks-300k-rolling-loud-claim-october-15-2026), and a record about freedom and the past is a better look than another argument. Listen and decide for yourself.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Baller Alert — New Music Friday: Meek Mill, A$AP Rocky & Gucci Mane (Oct. 16, 2026)](https://balleralert.com/o2og)\n- [Ratings Game Music — Meek Mill and G Herbo Reflect on Struggle and Success on \"Wanna Be Free\" (Oct. 16, 2026)](https://ratingsgamemusic.com/2026/10/16/meek-mill-g-herbo-wanna-be-free-review/)\n- [Ratings Game Music — \"Survivor's Guilt\" review (May 30, 2025)](https://ratingsgamemusic.com/2025/05/30/meek-mill-g-herbo-survivors-guilt-review)",
